ince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292807 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e5ae413-be1a-5211-ad08-178e5e19be0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e5ae413-be1a-5211-ad08-178e5e19be0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291107} :answer-field/id #uuid "2daa9284-83e4-5449-8185-db49a6c674e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d709123-c548-51c1-96cd-bc8ac660e378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d709123-c548-51c1-96cd-bc8ac660e378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291236} :answer-field/id #uuid "956ba8d7-fa47-5f7a-b145-9f5e1da669dd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292202}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d447ec6b-433a-5b79-9c9d-143f856c643d" :question/math-academy-id "q-275128" :question/problem "![](images/99/992be4e67316804381ffc38860d2eaf23fd4a93cfe22ec4918c30c41e34ade57.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{t}=\\lambda \\mathbf{r}+\\mu \\mathbf{s}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n\n$-\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nand \n$\\mu =$\n\n$-\\frac{5}{2}$\n\n." :question/worked-solution "![](images/c0/c0f7f4df52373ca602aff41c97a5b8413f510353874540b76147c527a2f4b18c.png)\n\nIn $△ORT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OR=\\frac{1}{2}|\\mathbf{r}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{r}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{r}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $RT=\\frac{5}{2}|\\mathbf{s}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{s}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{s}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{t} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{r}-\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf{t}=\\lambda \\mathbf{r}+\\mu \\mathbf{s}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{r}-\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{s}.\n$$ \n\nSince $\\mathbf{s}∦\\mathbf{r},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\mu =-\\frac{5}{2}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302254 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ca2060e-cf6d-5017-97b3-a1a9cc42949a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ca2060e-cf6d-5017-97b3-a1a9cc42949a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299998} :answer-field/id #uuid "163edb16-7a87-5fe6-a6a3-1683f24ab220" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301297} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a31f4f1a-a6a7-58a5-9b89-d256ec3e6ac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a31f4f1a-a6a7-58a5-9b89-d256ec3e6ac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300785} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ddb2ab0-ae40-58ed-89e6-151fc2b146eb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301426}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8fc6062b-82cc-5523-a4f6-6f883f485c18" :question/math-academy-id "q-326013" :question/problem "![](images/58/586fb01cd796c9d4e04aaeb393ea7f5fadd6c836d0b39d36c9c668447c490bd1.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{t}=\\lambda \\mathbf{u}+\\mu \\mathbf{v}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/2d/2d3a5c31af776cc49c2af118edc7256ca533320c7d53245593e5de6649ce03cf.png)\n\nIn $△OXT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OX=|\\mathbf{u}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OX}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{u}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OX}=-\\mathbf{u}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $XT=2|\\mathbf{v}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{XT}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{v}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-2\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{t}=\\overset{\\to }{OX}+\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-\\mathbf{u}-2\\mathbf{v}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{t}=\\lambda \\mathbf{u}+\\mu \\mathbf{v}=-1\\mathbf{u}-2\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{v}∦\\mathbf{u},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-1$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302255 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be2cc6e1-4dbf-5c23-8cb7-de5b9bae5093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be2cc6e1-4dbf-5c23-8cb7-de5b9bae5093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300912} :answer-field/id #uuid "189a9488-2d59-5b59-aa06-4aec634d9205" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56dacd44-2964-5317-a14f-0fd91f5fc60f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56dacd44-2964-5317-a14f-0fd91f5fc60f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300415} :answer-field/id #uuid "75e05b55-bce1-5c1f-891f-1a5c2be6e59c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301592}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90a7567f-3548-5a15-bedd-9db11178758a" :question/math-academy-id "q-326014" :question/problem "![](images/de/de5905301a41f02237a48257a79e457f11ad74186942ca5bcf0002ab041aff91.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{t}=\\lambda \\mathbf{j}+\\mu \\mathbf{k}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/1b/1be50e101b386f53ea5a2f1474f2e1d2debb8f98380d49a346dda32b37db70f1.png)\n\nIn $△OXT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OX=2|\\mathbf{j}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OX}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{j}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OX}=-2\\mathbf{j}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $XT=\\frac{1}{2}|\\mathbf{k}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{XT}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{k}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{k}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{t}=\\overset{\\to }{OX}+\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-2\\mathbf{j}-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{t}=\\lambda \\mathbf{j}+\\mu \\mathbf{k}=-2\\mathbf{j}-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{k}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{k}∦\\mathbf{j},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-\\frac{1}{2}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ff9eea8-3116-5c46-81b2-748e3985bd32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ff9eea8-3116-5c46-81b2-748e3985bd32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300195} :answer-field/id #uuid "13006d25-7abe-5d8d-9d49-2a380b810f7f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301287} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f65a6764-f098-5803-8dd2-cfae5e7bf3cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f65a6764-f098-5803-8dd2-cfae5e7bf3cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301177} :answer-field/id #uuid "944773b9-99d6-5a0a-bf11-9eeecd9281a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301701}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52ee4dd6-7ab9-5429-b0f8-a112547f6aa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-326018" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0c6dc7566d3ef4b0c047f048738aee6a204e0ba0e40cc48e83867456c6a1d67f.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/56/563522ad9e5cf8e134a6669364986de592c7d63da244b050ef466e9f6c971a39.png)\n\nIn $△OPR$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OP=3|\\mathbf{p}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OP}$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=3\\mathbf{p}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $PR=2|\\mathbf{q}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PR}=2\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\  & =3\\mathbf{p}+2\\mathbf{q}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}=3\\mathbf{p}+2\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{p}∦\\mathbf{q},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302257 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c9290e7-f63b-5468-915b-34a0ae957945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c9290e7-f63b-5468-915b-34a0ae957945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300256} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a110ab2-a48d-53ec-a75a-46f122a37820" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9aacaac-a578-58c1-8401-72795e01f089" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9aacaac-a578-58c1-8401-72795e01f089" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300965} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4ce281-3d77-51cf-9942-be3392d431c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301734}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2bbedc4-0ff6-53bb-b9ae-7bd7218983f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-326022" :question/problem "![](images/99/99d63eb31fba0757bde11dda3653e3791fcddb0b74b5325e20afcede4f3ea849.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+\\mu \\mathbf{b}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f7/f7acd51dcca9ad48f4aa7ec026beaeb67ddc9b1e88ab9b5042016674ba6ea542.png)\n\nIn $△OPR$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OP=|\\mathbf{a}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OP}$ and $\\mathbf{a}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\mathbf{a}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $PR=4|\\mathbf{b}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PR}=4\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+\\mu \\mathbf{b}=1\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =1$ and $\\mu =4$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cad88663-74d7-54b2-94ad-a6d1774885ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cad88663-74d7-54b2-94ad-a6d1774885ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300975} :answer-field/id #uuid "48daf202-288f-5a92-909e-f4da6828eaf7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb5f7c80-490a-572c-a55e-314ae670f1f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb5f7c80-490a-572c-a55e-314ae670f1f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301208} :answer-field/id #uuid "62599e82-fca2-5c45-9032-57359ac8e345" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301542}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1beeeaab-084b-5797-a939-fcb45aee542f" :question/math-academy-id "q-327074" :question/problem "![](images/c8/c8cbd5b93633e4e4899a1cde0da618f3be792bdbbd77db650c32814187b222f8.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/67/6708537b79154a7778fe52e8d82b6577f93d40a06d3af0267e3e4b7eaa6468a9.png)\n\nIn $△OMR$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OM=3|\\mathbf{q}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OM}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ have the opposite direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=-3\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $MR=2|\\mathbf{p}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{MR}$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{MR}=2\\mathbf{p}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r} & =\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MR} \\\\  & =-3\\mathbf{q}+2\\mathbf{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}=2\\mathbf{p}-3\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{p}∦\\mathbf{q},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-3$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302316 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1215840d-bacc-5fc7-b42c-e019593a22a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1215840d-bacc-5fc7-b42c-e019593a22a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300035} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccf56eb9-ff40-5f78-9ece-79037271fc6e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad4509e5-63fd-5831-b1d9-cb3cfd272cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad4509e5-63fd-5831-b1d9-cb3cfd272cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300830} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef617c89-4f69-5572-9be1-4c4fe8cc2949" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301989}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e61f5683-d5a7-570e-8d61-a9e450d0adae" :question/math-academy-id "q-327075" :question/problem "![](images/e6/e69402e97668c50f91258ca7e8dbb5206d1cd681e73bb9333303777adc866b70.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{i}=\\lambda \\mathbf{j}+\\mu \\mathbf{k}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/cb/cb8209592ec6d5be435622999c1b3eb86e1756cbe9852be0efdbbf41d41777ff.png)\n\nIn $△OJL$ shown above, we have  \n\n- $OJ=2|\\mathbf{j}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$ have the opposite direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=-2\\mathbf{j}.$  \n\nSimilarly:  \n\n- $JL=|\\mathbf{k}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{JL}$ and $\\mathbf{k}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{JL}=\\mathbf{k}.$  \n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{i}=\\overset{\\to }{OJ}+\\overset{\\to }{JL}=-2\\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{i}=\\lambda \\mathbf{j}+\\mu \\mathbf{k}=-2\\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k}.$  \n\nSince $\\mathbf{j}∦\\mathbf{k},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way.  Equating the coefficients, we get \n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2,\\,\\mu =1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "246b715e-1ea7-5159-bf5f-c1baa5326f61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "246b715e-1ea7-5159-bf5f-c1baa5326f61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300137} :answer-field/id #uuid "50fdf202-df72-5566-bc56-b474f1163821" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301493} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdfd483d-4c5f-5f30-9692-eb5855d0cc50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdfd483d-4c5f-5f30-9692-eb5855d0cc50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300988} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb3a4657-18da-51c1-a9cb-2dccd31b1ae1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302030}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c302ea94-ce6a-528e-80d0-db3b0e2f4650" :question/math-academy-id "q-327078" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c1a8cde010abbeaf318a64e6c9f3b6cbd3e7bac84babbcda4c1ebfb483fa2b2.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{s}=\\lambda \\mathbf{m}+\\mu \\mathbf{n}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/e0/e018cc5b4760b578d9ca514f9de6641e823bf5f6a8e17f019ebf24fc6ccb2248.png)\n\nIn $△OTS$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OT=4|\\mathbf{m}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OT}$ and $\\mathbf{m}$ have the opposite direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OT}=-4\\mathbf{m}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $TS=2|\\mathbf{n}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{TS}$ and $\\mathbf{n}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=2\\mathbf{n}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{s} & =\\overset{\\to }{OT}+\\overset{\\to }{TS} \\\\  & =-4\\mathbf{m}+2\\mathbf{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{s}=\\lambda \\mathbf{m}+\\mu \\mathbf{n}=-4\\mathbf{m}+2\\mathbf{n}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{m}∦\\mathbf{n},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-4$ and $\\mu =2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329675 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c24834-8cd4-5bea-b65d-b2c5663746e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327004} {:answer/id #uuid "43f90f38-cbf5-5d7a-920b-1121b5764f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327528} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7ece4b-a049-56ac-8617-bdfeb30b3311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328419} {:answer/id #uuid "b21ee6fb-0023-5a5