athbf{u}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{UW}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{u}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{UW}=-4\\mathbf{u}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{w} & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =-2\\mathbf{v}-4\\mathbf{u} \\\\  & =-4\\mathbf{u}-2\\mathbf{v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{w}=\\lambda \\mathbf{u}+\\mu \\mathbf{v}=-4\\mathbf{u}-2\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{u}∦\\mathbf{v},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-4$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cfbd0cb-8733-5454-bc51-0705f00c775a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327184} {:answer/id #uuid "453cbc37-f1de-5673-a82f-603e75313e66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327538} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb803a8-19e2-5f29-aee8-b53dd044f6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327629} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca86f5b-66fb-523f-889e-3c74b76af03b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327871} {:answer/id #uuid "c00cff55-58e1-5cdc-9c57-9569e58b8ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fb803a8-19e2-5f29-aee8-b53dd044f6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327629} :answer-field/id #uuid "11b673e4-f9d9-54b5-824e-58d311d04d42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329216}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/i