swer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c28aff5d-53e7-5f16-983d-538f4ce98117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365576} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cfd16dc-f42e-5638-89f3-68f27f774336" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81e0b22a-548d-5d2e-b32f-16412fc6cadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81e0b22a-548d-5d2e-b32f-16412fc6cadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365578} :answer-field/id #uuid "71b77659-ec75-56f7-ab9f-4c3596d182b4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365577}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "681d8619-9082-56b4-9422-241cad7644a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-326016" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f9ee37fe5f1cf32ba470b24e5d27b4164bd00a0caeae0536ae48d4cc5836c6d.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{t}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+\\mu \\mathbf{b}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/c9/c95e718a0c30e2be1f3678123eea0006b17fd781305c06a4f277488c2389337f.png)\n\nIn $△OXT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OX=\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot |\\mathbf{a}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OX}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OX}=-\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $XT=2|\\mathbf{b}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{XT}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-2\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{t}=\\overset{\\to }{OX}+\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{t}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+\\mu \\mathbf{b}=-\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{b}∦\\mathbf{a},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{7}{4}$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a9d3aac-2ddf-558e-9987-0dee3c2852ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2.5$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403880} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c5e6ea-81c8-564a-84fa-99f998a1a61d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2.5$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403881} {:answer/id #uuid "ed44e8da-0848-535d-a8ae-87bdbaa1daf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2.5$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403882} {:answer/id #uuid "8353c3d6-6092-5f38-bfd8-8a8168b1859c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403883} {:answer/id #uuid "aa67f058-afcd-51ee-97d4-c377ce896d7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2.5$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0c5e6ea-81c8-564a-84fa-99f998a1a61d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2.5$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403881} :answer-field/id #uuid "6554496f-6084-5a58-8758-7a159d646048" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403879}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8cb8830-d33b-5725-abf1-a6d3f309ef27" :question/math-academy-id "q-77452" :question/problem "![](images/16/1649e6c4ef2874cda2a7d7428b54220ef2a1790ba4b197c755165c48add0c31e.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+\\mu \\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7c/7cf17440c27765efb34b6a01c12a76ad4e980fc540307e2218227153661db5dd.png)\n\nIn $△OAC$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OA=2.5|\\mathbf{a}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OA}$ and $\\mathbf{a}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=2.5\\mathbf{a}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $AC=3|\\mathbf{b}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=3\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{c} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =2.5\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+\\mu \\mathbf{b}=2.5\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.$ \n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n$\\,$ $\\lambda =2.5$ and $\\mu =3$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420467 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f1fbbe3-94d8-5bd3-8727-4e6f9a832097" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420448} {:answer/id #uuid "90599886-7bfb-5b72-84ac-b60df87c5d99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420452} {:answer/id #uuid "a6826047-3513-5e97-9ed8-1ae795633fc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420453} {:answer/id #uuid "b05969db-3a13-5b96-96be-8b739e33d310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420455} {:answer/id #uuid "cf620219-7b28-5e23-a450-b4abd046ba47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6826047-3513-5e97-9ed8-1ae795633fc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420453} :answer-field/id #uuid "979e9c27-4560-5e47-8337-19ce5dc8192c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420463}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5f98ecb-0f26-50ae-9a82-cc334fd82c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-20413" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4bb7598c9ebae28be572508974cd025caa8f4a6c3313f025ff0f5ca55296334e.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $\\mathbf{h}=\\lambda \\mathbf{f}+\\mu \\mathbf{g}$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/43/43642acdb991827b4e1e16744e8a69507a383a1319ae07efde78480af4bab166.png)\n\nIn $△OFH$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OF=2|\\mathbf{g}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OF}$ and $\\mathbf{g}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=2\\mathbf{g}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $FH=3|\\mathbf{f}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FH}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{f}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{FH}=-3\\mathbf{f}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{h} & =\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FH} \\\\  & =2\\mathbf{g}-3\\mathbf{f} \\\\  & =-3\\mathbf{f}+2\\mathbf{g}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{h}=\\lambda \\mathbf{f}+\\mu \\mathbf{g}=-3\\mathbf{f}+2\\mathbf{g}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{f}∦\\mathbf{g},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514754 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd94222-3648-5492-8241-4b010da5c333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bd94222-3648-5492-8241-4b010da5c333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514759} :answer-field/id #uuid "01a589e1-3968-5f24-a7a9-df5b3459d167" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce52fb0c-e791-5450-871b-0e9a36cae631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce52fb0c-e791-5450-871b-0e9a36cae631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514784} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fd84807-e874-5f2c-879f-a22668b2264d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514760}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1d7e3219-6ed4-5e79-b442-f16e9eeecf24" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b6e5e69988b962627f39af49e25a904769a7de6bbebf8193e19d1540895ef992.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/6b/6be1c7aa854a75ea143bc6b0b70317128d3f83f7868db4eb1ad50b326d223b8c.png)\n\nIn $△OMR$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OM=\\frac{1}{4}|\\mathbf{q}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OM}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $MR=\\frac{4}{3}|\\mathbf{p}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{MR}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{p}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{MR}=-\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{p}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r} & =\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MR} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{q}-\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{p} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{p}+\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{q}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}=-\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{p}+\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{q}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{p}∦\\mathbf{q},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{4}{3}$ and $\\mu =\\frac{1}{4}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e30b8b0a-5c41-508a-800a-779854ec5eb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e30b8b0a-5c41-508a-800a-779854ec5eb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514787} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8b81958-e219-58a0-af4f-f9c9461153fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514777} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e5d37a4-d6f5-5dd8-8b8a-eac05883aa8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e5d37a4-d6f5-5dd8-8b8a-eac05883aa8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514763} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9f5d3fb-f5c7-582c-bbb3-23bc6fe37925" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514783}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4fd40f19-a244-5f63-bc0a-cb69c15f6c44" :question/problem "![](images/df/df3c05b58a8b6831ee666a527e80a506ed2b6c0a7c7046849689381c8afe2dce.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/ea/ea6d05ad928486c371f9d38aa0c8a8e3edc671a2e64c0426557e454e11120705.png)\n\nIn $△OMR$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OM=\\frac{10}{3}|\\mathbf{q}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OM}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{q}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=-\\frac{10}{3}\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $MR=\\frac{5}{3}|\\mathbf{p}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{MR}$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{MR}=\\frac{5}{3}\\mathbf{p}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r} & =\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MR} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{3}\\mathbf{q}+\\frac{5}{3}\\mathbf{p} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\mathbf{p}-\\frac{10}{3}\\mathbf{q}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}=\\frac{5}{3}\\mathbf{p}-\\frac{10}{3}\\mathbf{q}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{p}∦\\mathbf{q},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{3}$ and $\\mu =-\\frac{10}{3}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514766 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d233aea6-e46d-597e-8827-bc052950e6f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d233aea6-e46d-597e-8827-bc052950e6f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514785} :answer-field/id #uuid "36da8bde-6df5-53d9-839f-32d55e0e4394" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514758} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8978fe72-cace-5644-a25c-ae941745e1b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8978fe72-cace-5644-a25c-ae941745e1b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514774} :answer-field/id #uuid "b596270b-2f6f-5b28-a9f8-1ea62f75429c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514780}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "68bf99a3-7fc9-5547-9120-f2c14067205b" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c577ee7f4171d488642f9c8f9c8e4204269b05620ed22eae91db72b1f931837.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/01/0148dd6296370b01a9decbee10a96765be9af88c2f1eb8b9137d59131082c36f.png)\n\nIn $△OPR$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OP=|\\mathbf{p}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OP}$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\mathbf{p}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $PR=|\\mathbf{q}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PR}=\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{p}+\\mathbf{q}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}=\\mathbf{p}+\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{p}∦\\mathbf{q},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =1$ and $\\mu =1$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514769 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2f1211d-1dc5-5d77-b204-566c3ce70b91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2f1211d-1dc5-5d77-b204-566c3ce70b91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514776} :answer-field/id #uuid "0822b810-bc53-57e5-854c-5c75f04f62a9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514752} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68f2eadc-a64c-5b76-8842-987715ab90f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68f2eadc-a64c-5b76-8842-987715ab90f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514767} :answer-field/id #uuid "8483ba1d-4819-5745-a3f6-3c25e54d837d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514771}]