e {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514781}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb7bb682-766d-55d0-a9e3-945d7f1dcea9" :question/problem "![](images/06/060c4e83c464cfcd60303e524b142bdcc60e9a05125361d84babcdc4bbc79b41.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/d7/d7d81b7870205f722a1cc3d23131e573ead2cdfbc66ffcef81d75f31eac6c458.png)\n\nIn $△OPR$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OP=|\\mathbf{p}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OP}$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\mathbf{p}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $PR=2|\\mathbf{q}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PR}=2\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{p}+2\\mathbf{q}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}=\\mathbf{p}+2\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{p}∦\\mathbf{q},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =1$ and $\\mu =2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572708 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0830e01b-93be-55a3-ac87-38d68196c9be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572323} {:answer/id #uuid "1bd72a4f-8a2a-5d84-a5df-17bc127c8a72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572348} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed3d896-e6f3-5e0d-9156-7213b2534219" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\mu =\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572467} {:answer/id #uuid "a2644a20-0b59-59e2-bf9a-fb12db4f0be3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572490} {:answer/id #uuid "a306cce2-e35e-56e8-a262-e2dc8808954f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0830e01b-93be-55a3-ac87-38d68196c9be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572323} :answer-field/id #uuid "3810e182-6568-500c-b95b-e07cc9fea34d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572610}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ada3d5e7-07f2-5981-9fcd-59fe51195895" :question/math-academy-id "q-120273" :question/problem "![](images/5d/5dea155246de4f35697780db7ebf1802cdf5c2899fe42fa494993be2f65dd7f3.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $\\mathbf{h}=\\lambda \\mathbf{f}+\\mu \\mathbf{g}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/99/9905448ad59cb2f68f5def832811eb34056305d1a535f23387f4403a340cb8f8.png)\n\nIn $△OFH$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OF=\\frac{1}{2}|\\mathbf{f}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OF}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{f}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{f}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $FH=2|\\mathbf{g}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FH}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{g}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{FH}=-2\\mathbf{g}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{h} & =\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FH} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{f}-2\\mathbf{g}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{h}=\\lambda \\mathbf{f}+\\mu \\mathbf{g}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{f}-2\\mathbf{g}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{f}∦\\mathbf{g},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e8cd8a3-5848-5337-929a-567d0fe4c28c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572355} {:answer/id #uuid "58536380-845e-5010-b39b-f5e39e4c551c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572422} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a75f3a-4920-5e33-be0c-78e376d995c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572497} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1a8c24-4115-5d89-a601-bd095e5bfa7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572523} {:answer/id #uuid "e054b3a2-0eea-5210-8737-47555b3de52a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9a75f3a-4920-5e33-be0c-78e376d995c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572497} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e94447c-6428-5f0d-9958-0d3458e2b5ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572623}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eeb1828d-7e99-5d6a-aa95-0e286af84c7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-120265" :question/problem "![](images/67/6715bda9432c2ba3e61c31f436cd6b7608312da499bb4372944d25db6cf76090.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+\\mu \\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/89/8997fda665e4bba248dd19f5b8fe0d2a2524df341042271a0f8426e0ce152ecd.png)\n\nIn $△OAC$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OA=3|\\mathbf{a}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OA}$ and $\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=-3\\mathbf{a}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $AC=2|\\mathbf{b}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=-2\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{c} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =-3\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+\\mu \\mathbf{b}=-3\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}.$ \n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186582353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05da8884-0b84-53b4-be8d-0c4ee296a4ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581860} {:answer/id #uuid "5518a4f0-c680-5b9b-baf1-dcd20aab042e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581971} {:answer/id #uuid "84331dd6-6bc5-518f-b9ff-e7302d0e4b1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582042} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd54c5f-bc9e-5214-9bad-257eb4fdb6e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582086} {:answer/id #uuid "a8db350d-738f-580d-959b-caceb8c956c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fd54c5f-bc9e-5214-9bad-257eb4fdb6e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582086} :answer-field/id #uuid "b33f9199-1c48-55ab-bf55-87ed20786849" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582303}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a51e863-8cb5-5ea3-be4b-fcc4293d84e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-120275" :question/problem "![](images/cb/cbd0ffe0fb9e879f2a93557da1aef08622c9e048e14d83c4f4619cf5a1cd47bb.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $\\mathbf{w}=\\lambda \\mathbf{u}+\\mu \\mathbf{v}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/fb/fba4b74fde44c862267cd2c58852f4f829f5b07ead948b0c18d79e94f7d1c0fc.png)\n\nIn $△OUW$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OU=2|\\mathbf{u}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OU}$ and $\\mathbf{u}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=2\\mathbf{u}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $UW=3|\\mathbf{v}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{UW}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{v}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{UW}=-3\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{w} & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =2\\mathbf{u}-3\\mathbf{v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{w}=\\lambda \\mathbf{u}+\\mu \\mathbf{v}=2\\mathbf{u}-3\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{u}∦\\mathbf{v},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-3$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735007 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f01f5e69-1133-5d92-a2b1-b7709d266f16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f01f5e69-1133-5d92-a2b1-b7709d266f16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735011} :answer-field/id #uuid "d840e498-dfe3-51b4-9ccd-ed6271151a02" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735010} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4be812c-9f7d-59cd-90cd-daaecd99c55f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4be812c-9f7d-59cd-90cd-daaecd99c55f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735009} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbbec0e8-517e-5143-9c7c-3445f3efbc99" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735012}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c62a9e0e-7283-5db6-8603-4fc28da1e7a9" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram on a square grid](images/da/da826185105dfc1ec4e45b6b32c7a7da6da33bb1a27aed665f9b67fadae4128c.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector path](images/c2/c2bcb1d71d99d24ae325386c8b99146b5854c6186b0f25ce64bfe24cf8379ef8.png)\n\nConstruct a route $O\\to X\\to C$ whose first segment is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and whose second segment is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$. The added dashed lines show this route.\n\nA copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves one square right and two squares up. The segment from $O$ to $X$ moves three squares right and six squares up, so $OX=3|\\mathbf{b}|$ with the same direction. Thus $\\overrightarrow{OX}=3\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nA copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves two squares right and one square up. From $X$ to $C$, move four squares left and two squares down. The length is $2|\\mathbf{a}|$, but the direction is opposite, so $\\overrightarrow{XC}=-2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{b}-2\\mathbf{a}\\\\\n&=-2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, this expression is unique. Match each coefficient to its vector, rather than to the order of travel: $\\lambda=-2$ and $\\mu=3$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122433f9-4f97-5f10-b51e-cae32384b524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "122433f9-4f97-5f10-b51e-cae32384b524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735000} :answer-field/id #uuid "20403580-572a-5e11-89dc-40453809e0ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5a5c521-ee60-5fca-9da6-55ee3551aee0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5a5c521-ee60-5fca-9da6-55ee3551aee0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735006} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9ce837f-c214-5fa2-af1b-b6c1b4ed8c37" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735005}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d46199db-7d10-55ea-8f4c-bb6ccaaae660" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram on a square grid](images/c6/c6bc3baa512da1ef4f9fffc94d0f1069402f58828a9b8ff732a6b97b1543597e.png)\n\nThe dashed route goes from $O$ to $A$ to $C$. Use the grid to compare each part with $\\mathbf{a}$ or $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector path](images/5d/5d7bbadbc141798871c16c1175696cf27628e2966c84d2bb2f744ff65d527c71.png)\n\nFollow the supplied route $O\\to A\\to C$. On the grid, $OA$ is twice the length of $\\mathbf{a}$ and points in the same direction, so $\\overrightarrow{OA}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nThe segment from $A$ to $C$ moves six squares right and three squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves two squares right and one square down. Thus $AC=3|\\mathbf{b}|$, with the same direction, and $\\overrightarrow{AC}=3\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AC}\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=2$ and $\\mu=3$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83aa297f-c7f9-5297-b7ee-0b257f47927b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83aa297f-c7f9-5297-b7ee-0b257f47927b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735004} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a075dfb-65b3-55a4-a702-e92f22aba919" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734999} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30a82fd8-72e7-5e30-8121-4b7dc2972576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30a82fd8-72e7-5e30-8121-4b7dc2972576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735002} :answer-field/id #uuid "6280df77-f517-5e12-9966-be78f6d11a31" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735003}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fdf23a75-ec61-5ac9-a21d-3757ff6f8cb1" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram on a square grid](images/a4/a4e769a145f41df882458202f1e9540ea17580e3bd661236cd334c8c68478133.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector path](images/be/be23bdf90ef85ad1d8b373ca25d9112b6d574c316f729c90db4269bdc3984147.png)\n\nDraw a path $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$, as shown.\n\nFrom $O$ to $X$, move three squares down. The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ moves two squares up, so $OX=\\frac{3}{2}|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the directions are opposite. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nFrom $X$ to $C$, move four squares right and two squares up. This is twice the displacement of $\\mathbf{b}$, in the same direction, so $\\overrightarrow{XC}=2\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two reference vectors are not parallel, so matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and $\\mu=2$. The negative sign records the downward part of the route; a length ratio alone does not give its sign."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bafc4198-e4dd-5be3-8eef-1544cf656974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bafc4198-e4dd-5be3-8eef-1544cf656974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735257} :answer-field/id #uuid "67af80ae-b5e2-5643-b036-bd4bfa9471d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735250} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5551e412-bb88-508f-b002-4209bc9a6198" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5551e412-bb88-508f-b002-4209bc9a6198" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735246} :answer-field/id #uuid "df797a40-f4c2-5376-85ec-b5e6ffb94002" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735259}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03cb3efc-e3ab-52b7-b9e6-28cbeee3b50c" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/b8/b87f77266a2d44642d01744a5bdcecf42345dd5ffd26531eae5af7c77bea2722.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/90/9013b552fbf1df93e6872f3fd213f1c80e3d4c1e935dd2317f04d52b69d3cdd2.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $12$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $4$ squares up. Thus $OX=3|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-3\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $3$ squares left and $3$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares left and $2$ squares up. Thus $XC=\\frac{3}{2}|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-3\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{a}\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReorder the terms to match their vector names. Since $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $\\mu=-3$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735249 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c6554a1-f893-59fa-b799-8615c07ba1e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c6554a1-f893-59fa-b799-8615c07ba1e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735248} :answer-field/id #uuid "15939a3f-578b-5711-ac13-9f83da140649" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735243} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11ece49d-d9d1-5f19-8426-22db32ca5570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11ece49d-d9d1-5f19-8426-22db32ca5570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735242} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5243efd-720b-5e72-b636-4cf0286f5dbf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735260}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "628e7c86-511a-5a96-a42d-cd88be4d4559" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/6f/6f39fa0f0006ca782883fcd6ce5f5f687e8ec90cceb15d1cc5eda21cd0ba4c14.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/62/62405de33e197db1e8ef48b2d39c5909179e00c9b933cb8b2820101f0323cbb9.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $6$ squares left and $6$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares right and $2$ squares up. Thus $OX=3|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-3\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $1$ square up. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square up. Thus $XC=1|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-3\\mathbf{b}+\\mathbf{a}\\\\&=\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReorder the terms to match their vector names. Since $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=1$ and $\\mu=-3$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735252 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a080f58e-4c64-5ebd-8425-6724a800df69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a080f58e-4c64-5ebd-8425-6724a800df69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735256} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e3a506c-701e-5999-b79a-a6e1b6d3da3b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735251} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000d7fee-2d0c-5b35-a622-7b4fc6dae9dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "000d7fee-2d0c-5b35-a622-7b4fc6dae9dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735239} :answer-field/id #uuid "fccab4ab-59a3-5b6d-928e-7b07e5fd4a98" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735263}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a8a858b-29c0-589f-be68-44f29738bc0d" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/7e/7eea4d14d23ec6a08512837065a0e8c314fddde9eb01d8eac638d4c5e5e9e00f.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/45/458c5b35ce2448591cee94390f436cc0c835c14f79e1cab2c55e960cab1b6fed.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $6$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares up. Thus $OX=3|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-3\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $3$ squares left and $6$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares left and $4$ squares up. Thus $XC=\\frac{3}{2}|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-3\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-3$ and $\\mu=\\frac{3}{2}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735258 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8e7cbc6-3c65-594c-8f00-2776cc76ee94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8e7cbc6-3c65-594c-8f00-2776cc76ee94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735261} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bddc27e-c0b1-5b16-ab38-836a4a97464d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735253} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "323a4f18-57fa-5e43-a681-52cbc1ad5403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "323a4f18-57fa-5e43-a681-52cbc1ad5403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735245} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e5e3f91-05d6-5c96-a4fa-368806a9ce8b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735255}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc8e6b34-f02b-5448-931c-94334c21f73e" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/9a/9adcf4f0295b807efed07a34d2bff2eee01a5229fd367f026fed6de705c34199.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/2c/2cf0ee7b5174b6d89944b5e3d6a48086048362ad029235a7ded707f735f4b722.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $10$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $4$ squares up. Thus $OX=\\frac{5}{2}|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $1$ square right and $1$ square down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square up. Thus $XC=1|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=-\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\mu=-1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8521e6a9-96fb-5355-bf53-2312c787ab2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8521e6a9-96fb-5355-bf53-2312c787ab2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735254} :answer-field/id #uuid "197a1d8b-a301-58c8-acff-0cf49ece00b7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c71780-2ebd-5a1a-8b42-ea36774e7de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07c71780-2ebd-5a1a-8b42-ea36774e7de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735241} :answer-field/id #uuid "5805f0a6-69aa-57bf-8d79-b19cc88666c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735247}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb17691f-ad45-50d8-9bf1-066fefc0ee32" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/43/43d8df5853adab4bc9f7ae8138675c855dec0281cb0cd9b053539a116f8b20d5.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/5a/5a64645ccdb41247aafd9b4ffb99718662e93aae73ae498428e2ceadda8e2c54.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $5$ squares right and $10$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares right and $4$ squares up. Thus $OX=\\frac{5}{2}|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $6$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares up. Thus $XC=3|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=-3\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}-3\\mathbf{a}\\\\&=-3\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReorder the terms to match their vector names. Since $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-3$ and $\\mu=\\frac{5}{2}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186760546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ff5aca0-28dc-5d8e-ac45-131180a480cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ff5aca0-28dc-5d8e-ac45-131180a480cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760548} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d8fa572-dac0-5091-96c1-faab8f136f75" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e693349-85de-5680-b65d-cb589272212c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e693349-85de-5680-b65d-cb589272212c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760545} :answer-field/id #uuid "e97e2849-109f-5834-9bec-c4fef7a45e83" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760549}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ccc521b-cd0f-55f5-8aee-f604b35684c4" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/92/9237b017099fc15166673e8f9845d5aef871761499574352d736d3c0dd7da37b.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/e9/e97aaf366a2e97335af9df979f71d5123badc630a6d35e24d839e52e1124e671.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $4$ squares right. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square right. Thus $OX=4|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=4\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $4$ squares right and $8$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square right and $2$ squares down. Thus $XC=4|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=4\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=4\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=4$ and $\\mu=4$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Two Scalar Factors in a Linear Combination"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096653 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096452 :question/id #uuid "09d593cc-526e-5691-9a18-efff515eae59" :question/math-academy-id "e-4288" :question/problem "Consider the following diagram, where $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $X$ divides $AB$ in the ratio $3:1.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{OX}.$\n\n![](images/67/678ea2936b8a5b1ded74cb8a0875c629e8be0f7002c98492ebf2e8109fc603ef.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OX} = \\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AX}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\mathbf{a},$ so we just need to work out $\\overrightarrow{AX}.$\n\nFirst, from $\\triangle OAB,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AX:XB=3:1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AX}=\\dfrac{3}{4}\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\dfrac{3}{4}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OX} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AX} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{4}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{4}\\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735315 :question-generator/id #uuid "b9af5ff7-b069-596b-a18a-c20c9bf3c59c" :question-generator/script "generators/1d/1d7b9a9f843d8cbe259aa9211c6d45b0bdbf9af831552ed4c2bc5e505a200f03/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097046 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95092ddd-a592-51a9-a935-ee8d21d09f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OT} = \\mathbf{a} + \\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094250} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ea1899-3edc-5a44-a68d-8e0dc35e8f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OT} = \\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{a} + \\frac{1}{3}\\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094251} {:answer/id #uuid "0f332864-f317-5e8c-afc1-79039bba7d4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OT} = \\frac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a} + \\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094252} {:answer/id #uuid "149f3ec8-5bfe-5cff-b544-5450e508dd7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OT} = \\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094253} {:answer/id #uuid "28977d08-9521-501a-8c2b-abbc30e9104f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OT} = \\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a} + \\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094254}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba0bf42-9d3f-5ea8-846a-8da902ababbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094249} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bff8291-52e2-5378-8c8d-7d44f23a4c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364895} {:answer/id #uuid "34011083-f78c-5655-a0da-dc9cb40aca66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364896} {:answer/id #uuid "485389db-c4a8-5142-9541-d78c1ba0024d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{3}\\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364897} {:answer/id #uuid "3a64dc1f-5834-51d0-838e-b496cd2b0fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364898} {:answer/id #uuid "15eb2c14-0598-5915-a3c6-298fc96e1bc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34011083-f78c-5655-a0da-dc9cb40aca66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364896} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ab7ddb7-0e0f-504f-b6a0-52fbf88f18aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364894}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a844b5df-969a-5ad4-9ad2-fd01250ec5ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-12212" :question/problem "![](images/c2/c2406e6f3cb76f50bfcc73a348b38d93b7a24da8e4314e0b3523bb4cbf143364.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $T$ divides $\\overline{AB}$ in the ratio $AT:TB=1:1.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OT}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAB,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AT:TB=1:1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AT}=\\frac{1}{2}\\overset{\\to }{AB}=\\frac{1}{2}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b42e7ab-ac63-5783-9fe9-b799c27fa880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OR} = \\frac{3}{4}\\mathbf{p} + \\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{q}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095365} {:answer/id #uuid "92f11bab-00ea-5806-85db-1bdf7b4a1d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OR} = \\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{p} + \\frac{1}{3}\\mathbf{q}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095366} {:answer/id #uuid "ae89d302-f0f7-5e09-9194-c33771847064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OR} = \\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{p} + \\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{q}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095367} {:answer/id #uuid "db7890bf-209c-5d9f-a75a-7bb34f398293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OR} = \\frac{1}{3}\\mathbf{p} + \\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{q}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095368} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb7d370-156f-57c3-abfb-39c1d909ef46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OR} = \\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{p} + \\frac{3}{4}\\mathbf{q}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095369}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b1d5a5be-01e8-5ebd-96ba-2cafaf557859" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095364}] :question/id #uuid "27eb1507-c2b5-51fc-be8d-7ac00e5bfd55" :question/math-academy-id "q-42659" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb31653c9fc5031372c4b08e8fba0ec809c7e58a7a2321a8a7eb027b8eacd48a.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{OP} = \\mathbf{p}$, $\\overrightarrow{OQ} = \\mathbf{q}$ and $R$ divides $\\overline{PQ}$ in the ratio $PR: RQ = 1: 2$. Find $\\overrightarrow{OR}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256381 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d3914dd-4f9d-52fd-84b0-addb499fcb53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{10}\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{7}{10}\\mathbf{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253914} {:answer/id #uuid "491d5c09-aff2-5cb7-a5b0-ce88b63b18de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{5}\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{2}{5}\\mathbf{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254299} {:answer/id #uuid "8c5ace5d-136b-52aa-8a79-7ef14da799ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254913} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a748c5-34db-5f1a-955a-3db960e37efa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{7}{10}\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{3}{10}\\mathbf{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255540} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc15687-ab0f-5cda-9954-dc238979cbe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{2}{5}\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{3}{5}\\mathbf{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1a748c5-34db-5f1a-955a-3db960e37efa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{7}{10}\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{3}{10}\\mathbf{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255540} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae15c7d1-59b0-5d81-bcf1-1e0483cf8ab7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256236}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eee74ea9-5018-5a1b-8460-e61ca7767d79" :question/math-academy-id "q-120285" :question/problem "![](images/c4/c4d26b3db6446f586ca47634d9f9a3a004968a0081b8859ce46b4b4af799d066.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=\\mathbf{h},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OI}=\\mathbf{i}$ and $J$ divides $\\overline{HI}$ in the ratio $HJ:JI=3:7.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=\\mathbf{h},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OHI,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HI} & =\\overset{\\to }{HO}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{h}+\\mathbf{i} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $HJ:JI=3:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{HJ}=\\frac{3}{10}\\overset{\\to }{HI}=\\frac{3}{10}(\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{h}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{3}{10}(\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{h}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{3}{10}\\mathbf{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08042bf4-3ef1-5d30-b0f3-3f433bba0296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{2}{9}\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{7}{9}\\mathbf{v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253727} {:answer/id #uuid "0df1ebc5-6217-5105-bde2-c6c8741a810e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{1}{3}\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253788} {:answer/id #uuid "80614574-97e2-5043-b396-2114fd647949" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{7}{9}\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{2}{9}\\mathbf{v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254805} {:answer/id #uuid "bba72999-a4aa-5c77-bf97-584951bba851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{5}{7}\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{2}{7}\\mathbf{v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255344} {:answer/id #uuid "ded7e171-58ae-5dc1-8f0a-f9fdf6931af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{1}{3}\\mathbf{v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08042bf4-3ef1-5d30-b0f3-3f433bba0296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{2}{9}\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{7}{9}\\mathbf{v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253727} :answer-field/id #uuid "38859fb6-3c7d-5b36-af09-e8454c183c16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256022}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e34b700c-a9ab-5795-931b-c570187a69f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-120294" :question/problem "![](images/70/707beca1d856414e25874cc0b56c6654fbb41d699f01106b6749d49408b39aee.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=\\mathbf{u},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\mathbf{v}$ and $W$ divides $\\overline{UV}$ in the ratio $UW:WV=7:2.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OW}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=\\mathbf{u},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{UW}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OUV,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =\\overset{\\to }{UO}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{v} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{v}-\\mathbf{u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $UW:WV=7:2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{UW}=\\frac{7}{9}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=\\frac{7}{9}(\\mathbf{v}-\\mathbf{u}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OW} & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{7}{9}(\\mathbf{v}-\\mathbf{u}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{7}{9}\\mathbf{v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256386 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec7aea6-7e9b-5e22-b08e-4d9e29b49a14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{5}{9}\\mathbf{m}+\\frac{4}{9}\\mathbf{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253798} {:answer/id #uuid "38a55f08-30dd-5226-a035-3ef422cf9289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{1}{3}\\mathbf{m}+\\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254161} {:answer/id #uuid "98379f30-a71c-5d53-ae03-042f3405b7ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{m}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255015} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8a188a-e50d-5036-99f0-699a116256a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{m}+\\frac{1}{3}\\mathbf{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255178} {:answer/id #uuid "d0d7c189-608f-5823-837a-7c7d46640d1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{4}{9}\\mathbf{m}+\\frac{5}{9}\\mathbf{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38a55f08-30dd-5226-a035-3ef422cf9289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP