 #edb/ref 17592186514847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ae8ce9-f444-564c-b5be-bbe3c87eb372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07ae8ce9-f444-564c-b5be-bbe3c87eb372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514795} :answer-field/id #uuid "92e9c794-020e-5a79-a258-fed7b5ea3267" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991390d0-1deb-5380-8d75-2bd22dcc3a9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "991390d0-1deb-5380-8d75-2bd22dcc3a9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514827} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe4d97b4-fe1c-5bce-9cbb-ce2d601098a7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514849}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f73e6a96-1406-51eb-b8e1-7f0e1dc19d40" :question/problem "![](images/30/30350c72fc81e95a1287d9235974a3ab79f6e8d4bc11fa65611264c7ee115ebd.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$ and $T$ divides $\\overline{AB}$ in the ratio $AT:TB=1:3.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OT}$ via the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OT}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\mathbf{a}+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\mathbf{b}$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAB,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AT:TB=1:3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AT}=\\frac{1}{4}\\overset{\\to }{AB}=\\frac{1}{4}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{4}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186582357 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01e04c7d-dd4a-5ae8-baa2-1c4250593dea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01e04c7d-dd4a-5ae8-baa2-1c4250593dea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581854} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0a61f88-5e65-52a0-83b9-18a026bc77b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582322} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f03bae05-655b-59e7-b9bd-7be62003684e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f03bae05-655b-59e7-b9bd-7be62003684e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582203} :answer-field/id #uuid "f127bd55-0f8c-5a8d-bfe1-2279ad5036d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582337}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e2f6d0e-fbd4-52a2-bc5a-47ead1dbf4b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-322579" :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb43aa9d35e08f19fff74f030fc5246428b83f7bce907a890a3b8dfa62571dc2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OC}=\\mathbf{c},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=\\mathbf{r},$ and $X$ divides $\\overline{CR}$ in the ratio $CX:XR=6:11.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OX}$ via the vectors $\\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{r}.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OX}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\mathbf{c}+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\mathbf{r}$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OX}=\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{CX}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OC}=\\mathbf{c},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{CX}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OCR,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CR} & =\\overset{\\to }{CO}+\\overset{\\to }{OR} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{OR} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{c}+\\mathbf{r} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{r}-\\mathbf{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $CX:XR=6:11,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CX}=\\frac{6}{17}\\overset{\\to }{CR}=\\frac{6}{17}(\\mathbf{r}-\\mathbf{c}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OX} & =\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{CX} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{c}+\\frac{6}{17}(\\mathbf{r}-\\mathbf{c}) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{17}\\mathbf{c}+\\frac{6}{17}\\mathbf{r}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186734987 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d34ab49-50bf-593a-86c0-163dc06af6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d34ab49-50bf-593a-86c0-163dc06af6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734986} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8930110-b1a8-5ae0-985a-b298dbc7d773" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734997} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dab3235-ce9e-5f21-83c3-ee9512dc0e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dab3235-ce9e-5f21-83c3-ee9512dc0e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734993} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1192214-8a38-59c2-952f-2bc3e2893c47" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734998}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3125360d-8b47-5e6c-bbea-812b2836b4ce" :question/problem "![](images/d5/d58ca71ebfed4f3046819076ea6fc74da297e3e874188327de4753f9e3e1e154.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $X$ lies on the segment $AB$, with lengths $AX:XB=1:2$. The given vectors point toward $O$: $\\overrightarrow{AO}=a$ and $\\overrightarrow{BO}=b$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OX}$ in terms of $a$ and $b$ by filling in the two coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OX}=$ {{field-1}} $a+$ {{field-2}} $b$" :question/worked-solution "The known vectors point toward $O$, so their reverses are\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OA}=-a,\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OB}=-b.\n$$\nThe path $A\\to O\\to B$ gives\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AO}+\\overrightarrow{OB}=a-b.\n$$\nThe ratio $AX:XB=1:2$ means\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AX}=\\frac{1}{3}\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\frac{1}{3}(a-b).\n$$\nNow trace $O\\to A\\to X$:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OX}&=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AX}\\\\\n&=-a+\\frac{1}{3}(a-b)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{3}a-\\frac{1}{3}b.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe two coefficients are $-\\frac{2}{3}$ and $-\\frac{1}{3}$. Both are negative because the given vectors run toward $O$, whereas $\\overrightarrow{OX}$ runs away from $O$ into the triangle."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186734990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad91f864-8f25-5c80-b768-107534bd7787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad91f864-8f25-5c80-b768-107534bd7787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734995} :answer-field/id #uuid "271e6c93-779e-5988-9df3-d8e2b3e79c84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734985} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13bf9fe2-31db-53b6-ac75-80df442f8e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13bf9fe2-31db-53b6-ac75-80df442f8e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734984} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1e05ae-f3b9-5d16-acde-cfbc06ab8afe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734989}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c2fc166-4fc0-5591-b601-92d5bf18aaa7" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0b7754ad8bf465342865ba082a613c18d572273987e2486566450317ca804bc7.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $X$ lies on the segment $AB$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OA}=a$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}=b$. The lengths satisfy $AX:XB=2:3$. Express $\\overrightarrow{OX}$ in terms of $a$ and $b$ by filling in the two coefficients.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OX}=$ {{field-1}} $a+$ {{field-2}} $b$" :question/worked-solution "Trace the path $O\\to A\\to X$:\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AX}.\n$$\nFirst express the full segment vector using the path $A\\to O\\to B$:\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AO}+\\overrightarrow{OB}=-a+b=b-a.\n$$\nSince $AX:XB=2:3$, the vector from $A$ to $X$ is $\\frac{2}{5}$ of the vector from $A$ to $B$:\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AX}=\\frac{2}{5}(b-a).\n$$\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OX}&=a+\\frac{2}{5}(b-a)\\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{5}a+\\frac{2}{5}b.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe coefficients of $a$ and $b$ are $\\frac{3}{5}$ and $\\frac{2}{5}$, respectively."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186734994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "047e7256-a900-5298-ae30-30ee4bb5fa1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OX}=a+\\frac{1}{3}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734982} {:answer/id #uuid "0740322b-5cd6-5a20-a2f7-872248fe6012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\frac{2}{3}a-\\frac{1}{3}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734983} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad7fe8b-9562-57aa-828e-74b3ed1a1879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\frac{1}{3}a+\\frac{2}{3}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734988} {:answer/id #uuid "82abc0b4-e9ef-5962-a472-35d338d89ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\frac{2}{3}a+\\frac{1}{3}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734991} {:answer/id #uuid "bb44c279-41ed-5de9-ae39-26786f8080e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\frac{1}{2}a+\\frac{1}{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82abc0b4-e9ef-5962-a472-35d338d89ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\frac{2}{3}a+\\frac{1}{3}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734991} :answer-field/id #uuid "89d4fa47-018f-5bcc-b844-a7469ddaf479" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186734992}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "accb9340-cec8-58c2-8094-78507d92299d" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6a25f87080a52c536be8a179cf922bfddf0608a6d3933a6e99cb4b88a3babcf6.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $X$ lies on the segment $AB$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OA}=a$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}=b$. The lengths satisfy $AX:XB=1:2$.\n\nUse the path\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AX}\n$$\nand the given relation $\\overrightarrow{AB}=b-a$ to find $\\overrightarrow{OX}$ in terms of $a$ and $b$." :question/worked-solution "The ratio $AX:XB=1:2$ splits $AB$ into $1+2=3$ equal parts. Since $\\overrightarrow{AX}$ points from $A$ toward $B$,\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AX}=\\frac{1}{3}\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\frac{1}{3}(b-a).\n$$\nFollowing the supplied path gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OX}&=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AX}\\\\\n&=a+\\frac{1}{3}(b-a)\\\\\n&=\\frac{2}{3}a+\\frac{1}{3}b.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe larger coefficient belongs to $a$: $X$ is closer to $A$ than to $B$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63155d9f-94cd-5604-ae8c-e54170257816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OP}=\\frac{11}{14}p+\\frac{3}{14}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735295} {:answer/id #uuid "7052a1d6-5cf9-5174-bbc5-c666c23ee425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OP}=\\frac{1}{2}p+\\frac{1}{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735297} {:answer/id #uuid "ec4c7f6f-b46c-5288-9275-b9a02ffcfe57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OP}=\\frac{22}{25}p+\\frac{3}{25}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735310} {:answer/id #uuid "efa136db-5b5c-54be-85a9-98d824f6dc37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OP}=\\frac{3}{14}p+\\frac{11}{14}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735311} {:answer/id #uuid "f4712a5a-f8eb-53c3-ab18-591d2259affd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OP}=\\frac{3}{25}p+\\frac{22}{25}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63155d9f-94cd-5604-ae8c-e54170257816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OP}=\\frac{11}{14}p+\\frac{3}{14}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735295} :answer-field/id #uuid "95b1eb64-8793-59fd-8dc9-fcbc719634a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735303}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "348155ce-098a-5161-8b84-34cfe39ea95e" :question/problem "![](images/c1/c1ba013c40d2885305902a386c05c7a2080048537fd3d1d40e94cb367a4d8a62.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $P$ lies on the segment $VE$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OV}=p$ and $\\overrightarrow{OE}=b$. The lengths satisfy $VP:PE=3:11$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OP}$ in terms of $p$ and $b$." :question/worked-solution "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OV}=p\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OE}=b .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $V$ through $O$ to $E$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{VE}=\\overrightarrow{VO}+\\overrightarrow{OE}=-p+b.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $VP:PE=3:11$ gives $14$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{VP}=\\frac{3}{14}\\overrightarrow{VE}=\\frac{3}{14}(-p+b).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to V\\to P$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OP}&=\\overrightarrow{OV}+\\overrightarrow{VP}\\\\&=p+\\frac{3}{14}(-p+b)\\\\&=\\frac{11}{14}p+\\frac{3}{14}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735291 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cf3e75b-818c-51f7-a01c-8972b8795c9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf3e75b-818c-51f7-a01c-8972b8795c9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735293} :answer-field/id #uuid "18d2537d-0b81-559a-8414-4788a5299cd0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735289} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f973efb-3924-5d71-930c-5ce835f125dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f973efb-3924-5d71-930c-5ce835f125dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735304} :answer-field/id #uuid "a21954ce-4244-5f04-b3c3-2f44a99e9f7e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735305}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "369223e9-a114-52d3-a76b-95525ee905fd" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d75f291dcbcfa92bd92108934a7a536b6cd9924fa338b9d0f904413db778754.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $W$ lies on the segment $TF$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OT}=h$ and $\\overrightarrow{OF}=k$. The lengths satisfy $TW:WF=2:11$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OW}$ in terms of $h$ and $k$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OW}=$ {{field-1}} $h+$ {{field-2}} $k$" :question/worked-solution "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OT}=h\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OF}=k .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $T$ through $O$ to $F$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{TF}=\\overrightarrow{TO}+\\overrightarrow{OF}=-h+k.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $TW:WF=2:11$ gives $13$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{TW}=\\frac{2}{13}\\overrightarrow{TF}=\\frac{2}{13}(-h+k).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to T\\to W$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OW}&=\\overrightarrow{OT}+\\overrightarrow{TW}\\\\&=h+\\frac{2}{13}(-h+k)\\\\&=\\frac{11}{13}h+\\frac{2}{13}k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d77f645a-e092-5189-abf1-ee94f5e25dfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d77f645a-e092-5189-abf1-ee94f5e25dfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735309} :answer-field/id #uuid "0af1bf1b-3f5c-5c8a-9d19-efa497c350a1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735287} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3a67c4a-3f3f-5a4f-9d86-c871ded85fb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3a67c4a-3f3f-5a4f-9d86-c871ded85fb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735308} :answer-field/id #uuid "abbcbdd4-09d4-58f1-acba-940d905fd49f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735306}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fb609a4-bafd-5754-94aa-e8f02e85d14b" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e06141dfdf949b6ea66cd5445a9d781436484bab4b1bdd2c7707bc02d6a06925.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $K$ lies on the segment $HQ$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OH}=e$ and $\\overrightarrow{OQ}=p$. The lengths satisfy $HK:KQ=9:5$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OK}$ in terms of $e$ and $p$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OK}=$ {{field-1}} $e+$ {{field-2}} $p$" :question/worked-solution "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OH}=e\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OQ}=p .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $H$ through $O$ to $Q$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{HQ}=\\overrightarrow{HO}+\\overrightarrow{OQ}=-e+p.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $HK:KQ=9:5$ gives $14$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{HK}=\\frac{9}{14}\\overrightarrow{HQ}=\\frac{9}{14}(-e+p).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to H\\to K$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OK}&=\\overrightarrow{OH}+\\overrightarrow{HK}\\\\&=e+\\frac{9}{14}(-e+p)\\\\&=\\frac{5}{14}e+\\frac{9}{14}p.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bb7be87-cf23-5cbb-b353-eed0775db1da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bb7be87-cf23-5cbb-b353-eed0775db1da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735292} :answer-field/id #uuid "019e6506-bb4d-5246-928b-7699e809fa39" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735286} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f2455d2-43c1-5ac1-ae7a-a9c876b7afef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f2455d2-43c1-5ac1-ae7a-a9c876b7afef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735302} :answer-field/id #uuid "f995ca35-ee65-5df2-bd6e-34b90e866212" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735313}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "71218ce8-fcd7-5d9f-bfd2-75ec715e50ca" :question/problem "![](images/bc/bc3fc32b2c42ef44040a85395dc5795f85b9f2bf4c8e2b27df717bc9f3d51302.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $A$ lies on the segment $EV$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OE}=u$ and $\\overrightarrow{OV}=f$. The lengths satisfy $EA:AV=1:1$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ in terms of $u$ and $f$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OA}=$ {{field-1}} $u+$ {{field-2}} $f$" :question/worked-solution "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OE}=u\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OV}=f .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $E$ through $O$ to $V$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{EV}=\\overrightarrow{EO}+\\overrightarrow{OV}=-u+f.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $EA:AV=1:1$ gives $2$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{EA}=\\frac{1}{2}\\overrightarrow{EV}=\\frac{1}{2}(-u+f).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to E\\to A$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OA}&=\\overrightarrow{OE}+\\overrightarrow{EA}\\\\&=u+\\frac{1}{2}(-u+f)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}u+\\frac{1}{2}f.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1341f010-6241-5fb1-aace-698406cf545d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{1}{7}f+\\frac{6}{7}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735288} {:answer/id #uuid "6bbc02f4-15c7-51ad-90e1-d2da7608ef6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{1}{4}f+\\frac{3}{4}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735296} {:answer/id #uuid "7652cd98-5ae1-59d0-bc24-ba50c0def3e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{3}{4}f+\\frac{1}{4}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735299} {:answer/id #uuid "c6824edb-6742-5231-a843-b9dc1c67e2a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{6}{7}f+\\frac{1}{7}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735307} {:answer/id #uuid "fde94c3d-a081-5b40-bf18-6eba01284c55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{1}{2}f+\\frac{1}{2}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6824edb-6742-5231-a843-b9dc1c67e2a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{6}{7}f+\\frac{1}{7}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735307} :answer-field/id #uuid "84b23273-71dc-5752-85cc-3b72aa48c017" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735300}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86175cf5-30b4-50d0-9d04-18d042560a85" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2fcd54763ecfbdaf53ccccd7a5751a9c9f478db7403c8ee53cbb3b09d3e5e051.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $U$ lies on the segment $KC$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OK}=f$ and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=p$. The lengths satisfy $KU:UC=1:6$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OU}$ in terms of $f$ and $p$." :question/worked-solution "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OK}=f\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OC}=p .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $K$ through $O$ to $C$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{KC}=\\overrightarrow{KO}+\\overrightarrow{OC}=-f+p.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $KU:UC=1:6$ gives $7$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{KU}=\\frac{1}{7}\\overrightarrow{KC}=\\frac{1}{7}(-f+p).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to K\\to U$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OU}&=\\overrightarrow{OK}+\\overrightarrow{KU}\\\\&=f+\\frac{1}{7}(-f+p)\\\\&=\\frac{6}{7}f+\\frac{1}{7}p.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector That Satisfies a Ratio in Terms of Known Vectors"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096672 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096459 :question/id #uuid "b77c065c-3821-513c-9376-6e7108074616" :question/math-academy-id "e-4701" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=1 \\\\ y+z &=-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=1 \\\\ y+z &=-2 \\\\ z &=2,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2) &=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2) &=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049422 :topic/difficulty 1.18463012388646 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428274 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account linear: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: linear=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/linear-frequency-estimates.json, pair 151->148. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050765} :encompassing/weight 1.0}] :topic/id #uuid "f3a09ebe-2d8e-5a69-8681-eb398a98c3dd" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059775} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059776}] :topic/math-academy-id 151 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048853} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049058} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049409}] :topic/title "Solving 2x2 Systems of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757165 :question-generator/id #uuid "c1fd263d-f23a-529f-845e-b05d0e651c17" :question-generator/script "generators/d8/d82945ff96531751dc7c15d518677845ea6a4302922d36c404bfbc72f8d433f8/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096937 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2af7fa69-5175-5f82-abdc-7a83d1c7437a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414020} {:answer/id #uuid "3faa2fb1-77d5-521f-acea-30296fef736c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414021} {:answer/id #uuid "797daa95-425d-5598-93a6-9f8e22458433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,2,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414024} {:answer/id #uuid "a48bd680-d71c-5a27-9b6b-4fee3480952d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414027} {:answer/id #uuid "c64960b9-232a-5479-96de-e63c3bb0d15f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,2,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a48bd680-d71c-5a27-9b6b-4fee3480952d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414027} :answer-field/id #uuid "145fd237-737e-5055-9883-501b0228a34c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414029}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6f82ff82-f58e-5dd1-b2bf-5cc0bd58f164" :question/math-academy-id "q-10676" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 25\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 25\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -20\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=19 \\\\ y+2z &=13 \\\\ z &=5,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(5)=13\\,⟹\\,y=13-10=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=3$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(3)+2(5)=19\\,⟹\\,x=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=6,y=3$, and $z=5.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨6,3,5⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "046f428e-556f-5956-b78b-d2844abad4b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284826} {:answer/id #uuid "babfedb6-0dfd-59fe-83fc-1aade7621c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286487} {:answer/id #uuid "c1a979f3-bf84-5ce4-a382-9675dac8cb9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286562} {:answer/id #uuid "e3dfdeab-6885-5e75-a55d-ac0b26ea713b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286868} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ba7f8a-2143-5951-aadf-be80dd868963" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "babfedb6-0dfd-59fe-83fc-1aade7621c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286487} :answer-field/id #uuid "78caa516-f3d8-59a7-8c65-740773cd1cf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287404}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a19bbe50-faec-58bf-b57a-44ae8f766527" :question/math-academy-id "q-20505" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+6z &=5 \\\\ y-10z &=-11 \\\\ 4x+8y+13z &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11 & -11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{11}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "335c1d28-6ef0-501b-8648-2c0e5914f807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,6,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263444} {:answer/id #uuid "bda33206-a035-53c6-9921-6f6c110c575a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,2,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264647} {:answer/id #uuid "f4057cf8-6668-54c9-bf42-88c4d70eac10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265143} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ca4d3b-5b47-5683-9882-c5ab43df0469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265178} {:answer/id #uuid "fda5f85f-ead2-5bc7-84eb-7f79db911497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,6,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8ca4d3b-5b47-5683-9882-c5ab43df0469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265178} :answer-field/id #uuid "eadf5a06-1fa1-5b76-950d-e8ed3be547ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265664}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49125958-677d-58d5-ae65-4f5b3deb04dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-130926" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=-3 \\\\ y-2z &=-2 \\\\ z &=8,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=8$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-2(8)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-2+16=14.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=14$ and $z=8$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(14)+(8)=-3\\,⟹\\,x=17.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=17,y=14$, and $z=8.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨17,14,8⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb4f677-6e20-5d48-8adf-dad8e569076e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=8$ and $z=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285033} {:answer/id #uuid "67b6832b-f7f1-55d1-92dd-f7c48ee15a21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=4$ and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285735} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6c5f1f-a44d-56e0-b1b5-4ebcaafd017f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=6$ and $z=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286213} {:answer/id #uuid "9e0477fe-23d0-5b2c-af42-8e02c492ff15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=2$ and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286234} {:answer/id #uuid "bcba1021-c3fa-5be5-90b6-ccdceb2d3943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=5$ and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e0477fe-23d0-5b2c-af42-8e02c492ff15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=2$ and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286234} :answer-field/id #uuid "13c51648-1907-5520-9df6-2d1f4963b562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287184}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "76260352-1678-5f91-b36f-3214c8df1e0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-20263" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=6 \\\\ y+z &=5 \\\\ 2x+3y+2z &=14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 & 14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=6 \\\\ y+z &=5 \\\\ z &=3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=3$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(3)=5\\,⟹\\,y=5-3=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=2$ and $z=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(2)+(3)=6\\,⟹\\,x=6-5=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1,y=2$ and $z=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15719692-f572-52e2-92ef-7c37695a20ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284977} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb9ba6d-8ad5-5004-96ed-80c84894925e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286091} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5c7bb0-6725-548b-b664-64d4ff92c96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286504} {:answer/id #uuid "d6bbdd67-60e8-56e1-96f6-8012386dd066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286742} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e5b59d-43dc-5f6c-8987-626af7040c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc5c7bb0-6725-548b-b664-64d4ff92c96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286504} :answer-field/id #uuid "28841267-b70d-52db-841b-c4f0d84407a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287232}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e202a5f2-1485-54d2-ad75-6c42b9340de9" :question/math-academy-id "q-20524" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17efca8f-87be-5b95-8922-289fdb1d26ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285001} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4254ad-d231-50fd-9b68-9ebbd2ce5ce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285352} {:answer/id #uuid "45a723dd-0ef1-5ec0-b478-73144022c495" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285424} {:answer/id #uuid "75525907-933a-53d6-ae44-4d6d45f4ca9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285870} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf19ccd-17f1-5cf4-8f69-4973c62ab6fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c4254ad-d231-50fd-9b68-9ebbd2ce5ce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285352} :answer-field/id #uuid "51bb4809-5d86-5a66-b4a7-5e6d674e0405" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287329}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9aba0f5-8a1c-5403-81c5-fd64e80722c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-20533" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=0 \\\\ y+2z &=0 \\\\ x+y+3z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ae6737-5709-5299-9355-f610cf32cf10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-11,y=4$ and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284870} {:answer/id #uuid "38432a32-b421-5cb9-b804-edecfba79df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1,y=4$ and $z=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285312} {:answer/id #uuid "b532826d-782c-5acc-b69d-27c5cf349663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13,y=-4$ and $z=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286436} {:answer/id #uuid "ddb9a50d-a3e7-56d7-b7e0-47332e68cf82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-2,y=4$ and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286806} {:answer/id #uuid "f110becd-084a-5b17-b76a-616cfd4c91b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f110becd-084a-5b17-b76a-616cfd4c91b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286999} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b2ad410-5feb-53d6-a57d-187523cf9154" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287438}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00b50258-32a4-58d0-8a62-9857f481b38c" :question/math-academy-id "q-20542" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=-3 \\\\ x+2y+2z &=2 \\\\ 3x+4y+4z &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 17\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=-3 \\\\ y &=5 \\\\ z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=5$ and $z=-6$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+5+2(-6)=-3\\,⟹\\,x-7=-3\\,⟹\\,x=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4,$ $y=5,$ and $z=-6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1c26475-90bd-5e7a-84b3-47ac0bd01588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367937} {:answer/id #uuid "97a92173-cc7b-5847-916b-da911b96d3d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367938} {:answer/id #uuid "3f69175b-4c5a-5019-855c-5dd66c050c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367939} {:answer/id #uuid "135066fa-e5ab-531e-823d-7b8a43cfbd6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367940} {:answer/id #uuid "f54d27f3-bd4c-5652-a2f5-cdb2aeecffce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97a92173-cc7b-5847-916b-da911b96d3d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367938} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ee53708-7bbe-5275-be3b-4ffaa95c115d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367936}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8557cbac-c9fb-5ae6-8b4f-ab9d7e2cdf03" :question/math-academy-id "q-20515" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z &=-4 \\\\ 2x+5y+3z &=-10 \\\\ 3x+6y+4z &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e289daf-4c28-5e8b-b06d-9bfb29306c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,-12,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368704} {:answer/id #uuid "de191ec5-6dfc-5619-92ef-3ef733d0d523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,-9,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368705} {:answer/id #uuid "22b06387-1b81-5688-bd9a-ca492425a4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,-6,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368706} {:answer/id #uuid "c999c0cc-98fe-58fa-aacd-b8e42f127e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,-3,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368707} {:answer/id #uuid "52fa9cba-0e91-5d16-a4da-3d9fa8b32a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,-15,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22b06387-1b81-5688-bd9a-ca492425a4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,-6,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368706} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e1e8500-0044-5eb8-b6ac-7951b743cc1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368703}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38fec071-dd2c-5be5-8833-47ebc39dc16e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73569" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 3 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 3 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=1 \\\\ y-3z &=-9 \\\\ z &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-3(1)=-9\\,⟹\\,y=-6.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-6$ and $z=1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-(-6)+2(1)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-7,y=-6$, and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-7,-6,1⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf440d3-3fd9-55cc-926d-c8fb116cd60a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390369} {:answer/id #uuid "07658a20-9348-593b-a22c-bfd4aa0d76d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390370} {:answer/id #uuid "43daa5ce-d019-5af0-b38c-6fa388015557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390371} {:answer/id #uuid "ec19f197-25d0-50fa-b873-ca959251ea66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390372} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6061c2-cc6f-52e0-b686-f2b9c79ec854" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43daa5ce-d019-5af0-b38c-6fa388015557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390371} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbe07bb0-ff2d-54fa-ba57-0a37b56d9acc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390368}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a05ecba-dbf9-513d-af2d-03ee8f54c56e" :question/math-academy-id "q-20508" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8326c365-38e8-509f-ba26-6de3d26a5411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390376} {:answer/id #uuid "f0893938-c4dc-5b69-ac7a-20d7546db3b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390377} {:answer/id #uuid "98de7d9c-ac96-50b3-a7cd-2e1f0a084bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390378} {:answer/id #uuid "5d46c30a-315a-5f3c-9e1c-febc548b0a21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390379} {:answer/id #uuid "c961a688-8a1a-5a32-8996-3f5dbb760b72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0893938-c4dc-5b69-ac7a-20d7546db3b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390377} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a2efbab-ca3d-5dfb-bdbf-f29fc5964e47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390375}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b0ab2ea-5bc8-5361-b6e4-ca31cdf1350a" :question/math-academy-id "q-20539" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 9 & -13 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 17 & -26\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 9 & -13 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 17 & -26\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 17 & -26\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395769 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23b6f110-fbc4-5322-8a05-6366ff4c13c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,4,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395771} {:answer/id #uuid "e6302263-6554-5d2f-bdfe-094ceb26b042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395772} {:answer/id #uuid "337c9891-a990-5356-ae53-39e28e060932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,4,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395773} {:answer/id #uuid "12ab6864-c814-589e-8f72-328eeae44af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨13,-4,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395774} {:answer/id #uuid "fa67123d-ee59-563d-90e5-5d86c85b1243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-11,4,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "337c9891-a990-5356-ae53-39e28e060932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,4,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395773} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a758e48-dc27-560b-a0af-fd01b7ea572b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395770}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3437106d-95df-5058-942b-4f64c5179bc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-20512" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ 2x+3y+4z &=6 \\\\ 3x+3y+4z &=11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ y &=4 \\\\ z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=4$ and $z=-4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(4)+2(-4)=1\\,⟹\\,x=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5,y=4$, and $z=-4.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨5,4,-4⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640047 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "465bb88d-dadc-5911-8c4d-7846b9fa6e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=21,y=-8$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639568} {:answer/id #uuid "605c77fd-1233-558a-a16d-e4bbb6abbcd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=16,y=-6$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639605} {:answer/id #uuid "831be825-b278-5e4a-b903-6aab92a8b183" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=11,y=-4$, and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639667} {:answer/id #uuid "a56d0b83-6dd5-5a4d-b56b-22a892c7826d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=5,y=0$, and $z=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639720} {:answer/id #uuid "b0d6ab28-6a10-5b8c-99c4-ec237b93a4f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=6,y=-2$, and $z=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "831be825-b278-5e4a-b903-6aab92a8b183" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=11,y=-4$, and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639667} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c85d458-4e6f-5ba7-9d78-922c1faeb15f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639860}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d92782a9-48cf-5d80-a718-aa1e910a5af0" :question/math-academy-id "q-73568" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 6 & -15\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 6 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 6 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 6 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=3 \\\\ y+2z &=-4 \\\\ z &=0,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=0$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(0)=-4\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=0$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(-4)-(0)=3\\,⟹\\,x=11.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=11,y=-4$, and $z=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757131 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59fb0689-6a40-5ea6-88f5-88dcd2be0abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -5,-1,-1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757138} {:answer/id #uuid "a4d7cc88-27ec-5356-ab2f-4241eae931b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,-2,0\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757151} {:answer/id #uuid "b423739a-9cdf-5ab5-b29c-82761b9de429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -5,-4,-1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757155} {:answer/id #uuid "cbccb036-75ac-5374-bcbf-0c0f9255d666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,3,0\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757157} {:answer/id #uuid "df21cdf4-d400-5a66-9c6c-7183aa77e131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -7,4,-2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b423739a-9cdf-5ab5-b29c-82761b9de429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -5,-4,-1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757155} :answer-field/id #uuid "de1d7729-8374-5461-b59b-0d830bba8c5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757161}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2438d038-6bcb-57d2-878c-633cde7e585f" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 0 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & -12 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1 & 17\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 0 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & -12 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1 & 17\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{3}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & -12 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1 & 17\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1 & 17\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 11\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2z&=-3 \\\\ y+2z&=-6 \\\\ z&=-1\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-1 \\\\ y&=-6-(2)(-1)=-4 \\\\ x&=-3-(0)(-4)-(-2)(-1)=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -5,-4,-1\\rangle$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ad38c93-07cd-5a7e-ae45-97105d48226b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=15,\\quad y=-10,\\quad z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757139} {:answer/id #uuid "60bd6aaa-8de9-5e98-b92f-12d04ba04a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0,\\quad y=0,\\quad z=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757140} {:answer/id #uuid "9b653ab3-8822-587d-9cd3-8304ec45ee51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-6,\\quad y=4,\\quad z=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757148} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b52cf9-2924-50b9-9d23-d28c2609539b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,\\quad y=-2,\\quad z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757160} {:answer/id #uuid "f976767f-d127-5412-bc0e-45541a18f0fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=9,\\quad y=-6,\\quad z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5b52cf9-2924-50b9-9d23-d28c2609539b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,\\quad y=-2,\\quad z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757160} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a264913-315e-534a-93d5-edebbc3517c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757145}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ce1ee1a-a508-536a-9f4b-843284f94d9e" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+3y-3z&=6 \\\\ -2x-y+4z&=-8 \\\\ 2x-8z&=14\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -8 & 14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{3}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -8 & 14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -8 & 14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-z&=2 \\\\ y+2z&=-4 \\\\ z&=-1\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-1 \\\\ y&=-4-(2)(-1)=-2 \\\\ x&=2-(1)(-2)-(-1)(-1)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle 3,-2,-1\\rangle$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f325280-16eb-5f27-a13a-aa711ec34764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,0,-3\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757133} {:answer/id #uuid "4532b2f1-1767-5e38-b05b-f1d039e0e48d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -7,4,-4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757136} {:answer/id #uuid "75d46666-4df5-5d2a-99ea-8787312e2d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -6,3,0\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757144} {:answer/id #uuid "a0decd9f-cf78-51ed-b8af-df9309914346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -5,2,0\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757150} {:answer/id #uuid "ac8aa2ab-b24b-596e-a09d-e87a0e36600f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -4,1,-1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4532b2f1-1767-5e38-b05b-f1d039e0e48d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -7,4,-4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757136} :answer-field/id #uuid "68d836b8-99ed-51ec-bae9-e6a86ecb88a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757142}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "68b376f0-3740-52b0-87e7-4920036462df" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 & 18\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 & 18\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-1R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y&=-3 \\\\ y&=4 \\\\ z&=-4\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-4 \\\\ y&=4-(0)(-4)=4 \\\\ x&=-3-(1)(4)-(0)(-4)=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -7,4,-4\\rangle$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ab3678-94e8-5c60-a4f6-52d3b9de8b97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -4,3,-3\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757135} {:answer/id #uuid "839f617a-c4d9-5c93-a834-d4b285c62485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 4,-1,1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757147} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa9efa0-3aa9-590f-ab8c-6b8da64bb82e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -6,4,-4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757152} {:answer/id #uuid "ad7e83c7-bcca-5d35-b00e-3a52c535393b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 10,-4,4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757154} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d6ed0a-b99a-5b4e-9d30-6d690e4ba03b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 8,-3,3\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaa9efa0-3aa9-590f-ab8c-6b8da64bb82e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -6,4,-4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757152} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a8f0b45-acfa-5715-8b59-466322e206b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757130}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "829e2446-cf7a-560e-9d6e-68ab9fc9d67a" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2y-2z&=4 \\\\ y+z&=0 \\\\ 2x+3y-2z&=8\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-1R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-z&=2 \\\\ y+z&=0 \\\\ z&=-4\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-4 \\\\ y&=0-(1)(-4)=4 \\\\ x&=2-(1)(4)-(-1)(-4)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -6,4,-4\\rangle$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ffb54d1-c2d4-5624-bb47-c1eedf1a4c3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0,\\quad y=4,\\quad z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757134} {:answer/id #uuid "558ec325-59b1-5a1f-ae1d-e6e59834bf1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2,\\quad y=4,\\quad z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757137} {:answer/id #uuid "6e858f78-cdd6-5b8f-8187-1c579c3bfb62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4,\\quad y=4,\\quad z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757143} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a7f5df-3459-5757-b87c-2b2ffe2a6ac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,\\quad y=-2,\\quad z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757158} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b8a12e-a0c5-53c9-96bb-1c27d64cb096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0,\\quad y=3,\\quad z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1a7f5df-3459-5757-b87c-2b2ffe2a6ac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,\\quad y=-2,\\quad z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757158} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce13f12-edae-5bc7-8a4d-847b328940ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757149}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb8212a9-73fb-5459-9c36-b8d1c537a9d5" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+6z&=6 \\\\ -x+y-2z&=-4 \\\\ -2x+y-2z&=-8\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 0 & 6 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{3}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2z&=2 \\\\ y&=-2 \\\\ z&=-1\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-1 \\\\ y&=-2-(0)(-1)=-2 \\\\ x&=2-(0)(-2)-(2)(-1)=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle 4,-2,-1\\rangle$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757210 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5403c332-513f-5a0f-b87a-3b377d13526f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -1,-1,-1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757219} {:answer/id #uuid "b8c5ffa3-4582-53ef-b7d4-56999f45cdd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,-1,-3\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757229} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d5fb70-22ed-5d5c-bf75-f4c899c7c518" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 4,-1,4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757233} {:answer/id #uuid "df2005b1-f056-5177-ba3f-83098011721e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-1,0\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757237} {:answer/id #uuid "eead898f-3c74-5964-a653-384311e21129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 3,-1,3\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8c5ffa3-4582-53ef-b7d4-56999f45cdd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,-1,-3\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757229} :answer-field/id #uuid "790f7dd3-69e0-533c-980e-47fdbe90566f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757222}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25c3bf35-f71f-5823-a0f9-2edc8baf3cd5" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y-z&=1 \\\\ y&=-1 \\\\ z&=-3\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-3 \\\\ y&=-1-(0)(-3)=-1 \\\\ x&=1-(-1)(-1)-(-1)(-3)=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -3,-1,-3\\rangle$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757216 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1386bbc9-82ee-53ab-a4fa-5bd12d910e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\quad y=1,\\quad z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757209} {:answer/id #uuid "4185ec66-7084-5497-8d99-8b03931174dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\quad y=1,\\quad z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757215} {:answer/id #uuid "ada9317f-0ae5-509c-8d03-c0f19894a1d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\quad y=1,\\quad z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757228} {:answer/id #uuid "ca14b509-c034-5534-99aa-5f0ae0af43f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\quad y=1,\\quad z=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757235} {:answer/id #uuid "e108f8a8-8e68-50a1-996b-406dcfab6bd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\quad y=1,\\quad z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ada9317f-0ae5-509c-8d03-c0f19894a1d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\quad y=1,\\quad z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757228} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ea6622-4474-5a35-ba9b-779eb0ac99ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757217}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "41959785-204f-55d6-b359-c0c483175e9f" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=\\frac{1}{2}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y&=-2 \\\\ y&=1 \\\\ z&=4\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=4 \\\\ y&=1-(0)(4)=1 \\\\ x&=-2-(1)(1)-(0)(4)=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -3,1,4\\rangle$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757220 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fba1d50-9ced-596d-b9fe-c4406d96442b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 5,5,2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757213} {:answer/id #uuid "5006283d-5b05-5790-aeb6-350e0b79e28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -1,-7,-4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757218} {:answer/id #uuid "a2394689-8470-5b37-ba0c-bdb5cc3b320c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 7,9,4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757226} {:answer/id #uuid "c9735934-834a-500e-8506-a25562105899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-5,-3\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757234} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a9019c-29fc-58ef-a6f5-e766046ef89a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 1,-3,-2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5006283d-5b05-5790-aeb6-350e0b79e28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -1,-7,-4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757218} :answer-field/id #uuid "919b8f82-8656-56c1-a7a3-8ef17908ace7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757223}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "58bb7242-abb6-53be-8c5a-b994136e7d02" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y+2z&=4 \\\\ -x-2y+5z&=-5 \\\\ -2x+4y-8z&=6\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 5 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 5 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z&=2 \\\\ y-2z&=1 \\\\ z&=-4\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-4 \\\\ y&=1-(-2)(-4)=-7 \\\\ x&=2-(-1)(-7)-(1)(-4)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -1,-7,-4\\rangle$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757221 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28b12068-328e-55d2-ba95-022a6a59c2ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4,\\quad y=-1,\\quad z=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757211} {:answer/id #uuid "bfd7b7e4-5c77-5c9f-9414-c7365cacd4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4,\\quad y=1,\\quad z=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757232} {:answer/id #uuid "cf3dd81a-c7c2-5ab9-8a60-c88548a1edf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\quad y=2,\\quad z=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757236} {:answer/id #uuid "eb69de9a-a6e4-50cb-8795-ad2531fe2ea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\quad y=-4,\\quad z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757239} {:answer/id #uuid "eded3de7-0ab5-5792-97a2-e110af794c6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\quad y=1,\\quad z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb69de9a-a6e4-50cb-8795-ad2531fe2ea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\quad y=-4,\\quad z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757239} :answer-field/id #uuid "41163d3c-2778-59d4-bce9-d2631fc60e12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757214}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6d71b69b-78cd-5e96-a3e4-d78e12e36b10" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 & 14 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 & 14 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 & 14 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 12 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y-z&=-1 \\\\ y-z&=-4 \\\\ z&=0\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=0 \\\\ y&=-4-(-1)(0)=-4 \\\\ x&=-1-(-1)(-4)-(-1)(0)=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -5,-4,0\\rangle$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757224 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e77ef6b-635a-51ab-addf-958f96fad6f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 4,3,2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757212} {:answer/id #uuid "9e527a5e-e3df-54ef-b1ca-b8a91095047d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 8,3,-2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757225} {:answer/id #uuid "a2d25cb1-eb58-543b-881c-bea2f7224322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,-1,1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757227} {:answer/id #uuid "bb398185-8b82-5ee3-9332-bd52171be9ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -7,-3,1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757230} {:answer/id #uuid "be33199c-3d33-5cbe-9c28-11446814e259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 1,1,1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be33199c-3d33-5cbe-9c28-11446814e259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 1,1,1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757231} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae15f94-152d-5618-8553-a0933dae1a47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757208}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9678e249-bd15-5760-acfb-c81812d364cd" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2-R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=\\frac{1}{3}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z&=0 \\\\ y+z&=2 \\\\ z&=1\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=1 \\\\ y&=2-(1)(1)=1 \\\\ x&=0-(-2)(1)-(1)(1)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle 1,1,1\\rangle$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186760437 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44befbf4-438b-5985-9fdd-b52a14b6d297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760438} {:answer/id #uuid "5b78e520-571d-5443-bd88-1ef2aeb21e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760439} {:answer/id #uuid "8c11542b-c288-583e-9a4c-cdba2a0cbedc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760440} {:answer/id #uuid "9873543e-3bb1-51e6-9ca4-91316dcbf635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760441} {:answer/id #uuid "b13164d3-4c74-538d-aca6-ef70b2457cf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44befbf4-438b-5985-9fdd-b52a14b6d297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760438} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9d2e3a9-659e-5f91-b389-146703618f0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760443}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14147a5c-c74f-5281-a5a4-f0bd6e7662d3" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z&=1 \\\\ -x-y-z&=3 \\\\ x+2y+3z&=4\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186760446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b3020b5-5dfb-552f-b6c2-e9b993c1c77a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-15,\\quad y=11,\\quad z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760447} {:answer/id #uuid "84e5acb6-e635-548f-8259-f0a188d95fcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-11,\\quad y=7,\\quad z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760448} {:answer/id #uuid "b23eacb1-84c8-5b1d-9b23-56c0ad613c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\quad y=-1,\\quad z=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760449} {:answer/id #uuid "c14fd8d6-5d92-5110-a42f-921ca7be3ad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\quad y=1,\\quad z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760450} {:answer/id #uuid "c81af617-4ca1-5cd6-a286-62931f17605d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\quad y=-3,\\quad z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b23eacb1-84c8-5b1d-9b23-56c0ad613c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\quad y=-1,\\quad z=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760449} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed8720c9-07f9-5eb4-a1ac-ae2c8af1c83a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760452}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5502ece7-3750-5dc2-a5c4-e37a56f57a47" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x-4y+4z&=2 \\\\ x-y+4z&=-10 \\\\ 2x+6y-5z&=-2\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -4 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -5 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -5 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2-R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -5 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=\\frac{1}{3}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z&=-1 \\\\ y-2z&=3 \\\\ z&=-2\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-2 \\\\ y&=3-(-2)(-2)=-1 \\\\ x&=-1-(2)(-1)-(-2)(-2)=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -3,-1,-2\\rangle$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096673 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096460 :question/id #uuid "7760b6ce-91fb-5ba6-beb2-c244d6a73d69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4702" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=-2 \\\\ x+y+2z &=-1 \\\\ x+2y+z &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n\n\n$$\nM= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=-2 \\\\ y &=3 \\\\ z &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1) &=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757033 :question-generator/id #uuid "98dda97a-0c34-5d23-8a2e-9660f5991a11" :question-generator/script "generators/7a/7abf2c7dfdd446626f3a453874c25e6568f7196510aed61eaf19bbb3e7b019d2/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38b8de74-9b19-5fcb-86d1-d4eb77627541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339638} {:answer/id #uuid "82fe070f-9ba8-572e-807f-b7e3a637c60e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1$, $y=2$, and $z=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340305} {:answer/id #uuid "98a029ca-6087-5b72-9ca2-e3147cdb70a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=-5$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340507} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e3c2ea-d16f-581b-9b65-22d05f5e48ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=5$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341062} {:answer/id #uuid "e383876d-902d-5a68-82a6-fe6aedf0fd52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1$, $y=-6$, and $z=-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38b8de74-9b19-5fcb-86d1-d4eb77627541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339638} :answer-field/id #uuid "18caed8a-a8c5-5f22-b7e0-3310a888fea7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341425}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cdba1d21-3eaf-575a-9b38-07c8181fcd34" :question/math-academy-id "q-73396" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=8 \\\\ -2x+2y-3z &=-11 \\\\ x+z &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=8 \\\\ y-z &=1 \\\\ z &=5,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(5) &=1\\,⟹\\,y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=6$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(6)+2(5) &=8\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097350 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "affc0ad4-801a-5399-8a47-b7526facc7d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403628} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb21bbb-79ee-5df3-9904-5df560da18c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403629} {:answer/id #uuid "c5805566-431b-59b1-b5d4-027282fdf8a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403630} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4c1b86-80d7-59f5-af00-319d8bf12b68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403631} {:answer/id #uuid "76bc4cc9-6acc-5be4-bff8-66f385a06fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -5\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae4c1b86-80d7-59f5-af00-319d8bf12b68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403631} :answer-field/id #uuid "f15e152b-e602-5625-9a15-cb468ccf6dd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403627}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e85abf79-3b58-57ed-b3d6-9f31cc3b2817" :question/math-academy-id "q-73397" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $-\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "543df558-b8a5-545b-b160-2fe37379c9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263727} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb8ac6b-fce4-57dc-8d57-746bdda1d0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263931} {:answer/id #uuid "c42f8e88-729f-5ad1-b070-bff1132c48a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264714} {:answer/id #uuid "c483a5fe-745e-59db-8de7-5c8a3454d240" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264721} {:answer/id #uuid "d70a50c5-13c6-5393-8129-945ea4016aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bb8ac6b-fce4-57dc-8d57-746bdda1d0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263931} :answer-field/id #uuid "091832d1-1a63-50c1-8342-a7864cc522dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265260}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f61c846d-507f-5371-aeef-030ef902e9e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130928" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{7}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d3cb3a6-9b25-5f14-b7fe-ef0f81082c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=9$, $y=9$, and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339832} {:answer/id #uuid "6637df9f-50f4-58dd-8cf1-2dded102c657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340027} {:answer/id #uuid "82ffd466-0e67-5425-9c00-af468a2c3588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-89$, $y=-47$, and $z=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340306} {:answer/id #uuid "af2f918c-cf0f-5b21-8e87-4c608c0f9852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-33$, $y=-15$, and $z=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340724} {:answer/id #uuid "c76cf58e-617a-5441-8169-40443447226f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=142$, $y=85$, and $z=22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6637df9f-50f4-58dd-8cf1-2dded102c657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340027} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf34cc2-5873-5eaf-970b-9dc56a73754a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341457}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4fabb78b-3a40-50c6-9149-8d79603a31f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73579" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+6y-3z &=18 \\\\ -4x+8y-3z &=2 \\\\ y-4z &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=-6 \\\\ y-4z &=-3 \\\\ z &=-22,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=-22$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4(-22) &=-3\\,⟹\\,y=-91.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-91$ and $z=-22$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2(-91)+(-22) &=-6\\,⟹\\,x=-166.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c85a87-f9d3-5992-bd65-769c46e1d92d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,-8,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339203} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbe2b87-90d4-5154-8a7b-4cbe5d76ee8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339272} {:answer/id #uuid "266e54c3-4543-5283-9017-83d16e10e193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨25,-18,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339463} {:answer/id #uuid "32af4883-fe55-53ee-8722-a0f084a72e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339575} {:answer/id #uuid "79208760-a400-5994-ac65-f0b5469feeb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-17,12,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fbe2b87-90d4-5154-8a7b-4cbe5d76ee8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339272} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0944fb0-08b1-53ae-b7d8-bc6730da208f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341713}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3624bdf6-d1bf-5873-8a2a-1542d72f9250" :question/math-academy-id "q-73584" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-2z &=3 \\\\ y+5z &=-8 \\\\ z &=4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5(4) &=-8\\,⟹\\,y=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-28$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(-28)-2(4) &=3\\,⟹\\,x=39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=39$, $y=-28$, and $z=4.$ Or, in vector form $⟨39,-28,4⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f84b955-e25e-5955-8a2a-87d8b550463b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨52,21,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339543} {:answer/id #uuid "304cea0c-89a4-55c8-b0d0-dffbc12bb18b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339549} {:answer/id #uuid "35874527-0d05-510c-938e-52c64b49f406" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339602} {:answer/id #uuid "57014e05-78ee-56aa-a36c-1a4147653d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-58,-23,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339924} {:answer/id #uuid "e70f0c3f-b109-5746-a6d9-5b910dad1d5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57014e05-78ee-56aa-a36c-1a4147653d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-58,-23,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339924} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5f662ab-5ce0-5cde-8194-11854041cc57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341727}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a6417a9-7e20-54a9-9651-61368745cde5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73588" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z &=-2 \\\\ y+2z &=-1 \\\\ z &=11,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=11$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(11) &=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-23$ and $z=11$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-23)+3(11) &=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-58.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-58$, $y=-23$, and $z=11.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-58,-23,11⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061b84d7-0a88-5827-a09a-0ae94645e28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339179} {:answer/id #uuid "3493c0b1-471a-5165-b338-34b981a66bfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339595} {:answer/id #uuid "3670b23e-82b8-5a09-8d82-457c528c5b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339614} {:answer/id #uuid "b35d9857-7680-5d0d-9437-cc48d8d3277a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340757} {:answer/id #uuid "bd407622-a505-57f5-ad35-f323345504ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "061b84d7-0a88-5827-a09a-0ae94645e28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339179} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa4b0ec2-bc66-5a30-b57d-09c5803067da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341676}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7ecd0e17-9926-5c80-9527-2ab263ac9de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73592" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-6y+3z &=-6 \\\\ 2x-4y+3z &=-1 \\\\ 2y-4z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9341f62-c8f8-570d-80c8-63278f533fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13$, $y=4$, and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368711} {:answer/id #uuid "cf00639b-8c94-5353-94da-3f2b856bf365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368712} {:answer/id #uuid "48282e37-d5c2-509a-8252-6ee2a8e03b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368713} {:answer/id #uuid "3baa2212-ba77-51f2-be2f-5e043a5564f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=10$, $y=3$, and $z=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368714} {:answer/id #uuid "da3d5251-f525-5757-9a3a-816f522e1513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=16$, $y=5$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48282e37-d5c2-509a-8252-6ee2a8e03b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368713} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc8d2c28-de03-52ea-8fb5-2bfbbb958a9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368710}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f809106-1e50-5a91-813a-0a376c6d5c21" :question/math-academy-id "q-73587" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=1 \\\\ y-z &=-4 \\\\ z &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(1) &=-4\\,⟹\\,y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3(-3) &=1\\,⟹\\,x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29e0739b-acd3-5213-baab-e978002551c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-12$, $y=6$, and $z=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400515} {:answer/id #uuid "09aec1aa-dcc4-5694-820b-48b65b045141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400516} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea67907-7f4c-52b6-b879-e7a1aaa740f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-12$, $y=-10$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400517} {:answer/id #uuid "06e6ab1e-4b01-5e52-ba1d-2553cc1a9411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-6$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400518} {:answer/id #uuid "fc215d6c-0ef8-5f56-9172-bb0f8dae360e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=18$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09aec1aa-dcc4-5694-820b-48b65b045141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400516} :answer-field/id #uuid "924e4677-652c-5aa5-ad82-4e9a728fb938" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400514}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8eff9d12-5ab8-5d85-973e-0e821294f176" :question/math-academy-id "q-130927" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=4 \\\\ -3x-6y+4z &=-8 \\\\ 3x+7y-z &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=4 \\\\ y+2z &=-2 \\\\ z &=4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(4) &=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-10$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(-10)-(4) &=4\\,⟹\\,x=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403654 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bbb2c9b-2424-5248-830c-2c1f0a65a08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403656} {:answer/id #uuid "090537bb-6f40-5836-9945-a970355e758b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403657} {:answer/id #uuid "fab64420-cace-555b-aa98-7c62e22daa9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403658} {:answer/id #uuid "bb59ea2b-37e2-5ba0-85a8-5281bf3bc593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403659} {:answer/id #uuid "24b18c66-2b96-5dd6-a905-03f61b72ec8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb59ea2b-37e2-5ba0-85a8-5281bf3bc593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403659} :answer-field/id #uuid "45e63128-e41c-54ad-afda-6808e4f902e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403655}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "09ed8746-0452-52a7-a619-929b2d587f13" :question/math-academy-id "q-73580" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1111935c-e645-5bcc-9a24-5310e4abf00c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414019} {:answer/id #uuid "48cbaac4-0396-5dd0-87a0-2f04eaf0760f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414022} {:answer/id #uuid "70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414023} {:answer/id #uuid "8b765cfb-d1ea-559d-a6ff-8457bb546f81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414025} {:answer/id #uuid "979ac4ef-5db7-5cde-816c-7fb542951f8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414023} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa000c8-106a-5c36-ab34-ed3791f10731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414030}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "db1a0a35-4ef3-5f5a-8985-ee685a957f6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73593" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+6y-3z &=-1 \\\\ -2x-12y+8z &=1 \\\\ -x-5y+4z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bebd905-0240-52d0-968d-938c33de08ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-18,8,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639474} {:answer/id #uuid "0fcc8ddf-a247-5188-81f5-991e48007571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,4,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639483} {:answer/id #uuid "315919a9-e034-5a79-858b-4903e68687b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-24,10,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639542} {:answer/id #uuid "e0af81a2-e277-564c-87e2-cbf9fa1b30ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨26,-8,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639804} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e5c542-626e-5e72-9e3a-2d14fb66fe15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨16,-5,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "315919a9-e034-5a79-858b-4903e68687b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-24,10,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639542} :answer-field/id #uuid "da5c3e10-a3dc-5dae-b3e7-e412d2853970" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639936}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2dc08be3-c769-502f-bf78-0a4feb848af1" :question/math-academy-id "q-73577" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+4y-4z &=4 \\\\ x+2y-z &=-1 \\\\ y+3z &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z &=2 \\\\ y+3z &=1 \\\\ z &=-3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=-3$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+3(-3) &=1\\,⟹\\,y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=10$ and $z=-3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(10)-2(-3) &=2\\,⟹\\,x=-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-24$, $y=10$, and $z=-3.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-24,10,-3⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186756998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adceadb7-5698-5ba3-902e-3bc7bf839851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757016} {:answer/id #uuid "b96201b0-44c1-5e5e-b110-e196c1c857ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757019} {:answer/id #uuid "bb949d01-f847-5ae2-a5c9-c568c6e81646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757020} {:answer/id #uuid "bd52b8f1-4ca5-5518-ab79-c36e482b621a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757022} {:answer/id #uuid "cb015c85-9906-5b23-bc3c-38b140fe3654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b96201b0-44c1-5e5e-b110-e196c1c857ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757019} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd22473-befe-55a6-be59-70afec1d15ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757008}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "060af8c1-e26e-579e-83e1-d0f6c0b2b802" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-9y &=0 \\\\ 2x+6y-z &=3 \\\\ -2x-7y+z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form. Select the resulting augmented matrix." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & -9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize the first pivot with $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_2:=-1R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_3:=-1R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d47904-1296-51da-99b5-2d7d8575f749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-9,-1,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757005} {:answer/id #uuid "68ec9139-afcc-51b3-be24-48c4d0a19616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4,2,-1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757010} {:answer/id #uuid "75a05541-0e8a-508b-83dc-752a1abe700d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-17,-5,-1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757012} {:answer/id #uuid "b547149b-af32-578e-a9da-412f7702ead7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(7,3,-1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757017} {:answer/id #uuid "b7eebee3-ed29-5809-9209-75aca5191cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-18,-4,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7eebee3-ed29-5809-9209-75aca5191cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-18,-4,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757018} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6b99498-3513-5396-b1c9-949fc609cc72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757029}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63a85e4a-d05b-5eca-9202-d889f4d8cbfb" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+3y+2z &=0 \\\\ x-3y-3z &=3 \\\\ -2x+8y+2z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize the first pivot with $R_1:=-1R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_2:=\\frac{1}{2}R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_3:=-1R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=-3 \\\\ y &=-1-(-1)(-3) \\\\ &=-4 \\\\ x &=0-(-3)(-4) \\\\ &\\quad -(-2)(-3) \\\\ &=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(-18,-4,-3\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a92d1d9-fdda-5f46-853c-c8b923efd984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(9,11,-4\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757000} {:answer/id #uuid "101b969b-d8da-52ab-a407-81ff7e527c18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-25,-6,-4\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757001} {:answer/id #uuid "10364258-1db9-5415-abc9-6d0450049b00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-13,-2,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757002} {:answer/id #uuid "c0cb3cbf-d0b3-54ba-8781-cc85989a6162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-7,3,-4\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757025} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe56609-eae4-5504-a3c9-85797c67870f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(5,7,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0cb3cbf-d0b3-54ba-8781-cc85989a6162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-7,3,-4\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757025} :answer-field/id #uuid "6be22918-8ee0-5a73-afb2-9024d55d9c45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757011}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87c67b19-2b31-5c31-a830-94bab02c0bf2" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ for the variables $x,y,z$ in that order.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize the first pivot with $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_2:=\\frac{1}{3}R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=-4 \\\\ y &=3-(0)(-4) \\\\ &=3 \\\\ x &=-5-(-2)(3) \\\\ &\\quad -(-2)(-4) \\\\ &=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(-7,3,-4\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a5b4d5-96d1-59db-98b3-7055a705a173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-19,-7,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186756999} {:answer/id #uuid "1783fe2f-7350-5ac6-8a27-09a181249294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(19,5,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757003} {:answer/id #uuid "bdca9560-7b65-5003-a5b1-a32fc045a0f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(8,2,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757023} {:answer/id #uuid "cdaab2c7-b756-502b-8030-f13732b39ade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-2,-2,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757027} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f172c4-e666-55ff-8830-72a7d1816a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-5,-3,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1783fe2f-7350-5ac6-8a27-09a181249294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(19,5,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757003} :answer-field/id #uuid "36100d49-b552-5d7b-9be2-ba1fc3ffd73f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757006}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8dc5d6c8-0139-5220-8d45-fe4bded0ce05" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+9y+3z &=-12 \\\\ 2x-6y-4z &=8 \\\\ -2x+4y-2z &=-18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 9 & 3 & -12 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -18\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize the first pivot with $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -18\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -18\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & -10\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_2:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=0 \\\\ y &=5-(2)(0) \\\\ &=5 \\\\ x &=4-(-3)(5) \\\\ &\\quad -(-1)(0) \\\\ &=19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(19,5,0\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37ff0381-67d3-5998-91a0-45a3dc47d372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757007} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5cb553-8022-5fc5-ba89-35bfbc9a047f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757015} {:answer/id #uuid "be84635e-2b68-5138-9d17-5e5c90fee3a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757024} {:answer/id #uuid "df8a3a8c-3067-5b41-95ac-40631027eacc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757030} {:answer/id #uuid "f75fcf2d-06d5-5b73-a43b-36567f429da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be84635e-2b68-5138-9d17-5e5c90fee3a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757024} :answer-field/id #uuid "272d888d-babf-527e-8bc4-c16889c578ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd4bec18-420e-5a7e-8c05-e86723f9ab68" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ for the variables $x,y,z$ in that order.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -4 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form. Select the resulting augmented matrix." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -4 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize the first pivot with $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_2:=\\frac{1}{2}R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c5babc5-f223-5d99-84f1-f4807792f441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757046} {:answer/id #uuid "54892b6a-9372-5cdc-8728-12e0bec7a0ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757047} {:answer/id #uuid "950ad8a3-a6d6-5f53-b29b-81823a881765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757055} {:answer/id #uuid "95671fe6-b2f1-512d-b5c8-38b2ceff74fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757056} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb84122-f6f7-5e29-9722-43d66cbe3890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c5babc5-f223-5d99-84f1-f4807792f441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757046} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff140869-99be-5530-a54f-fac57d81520e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757068}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d6b8129-3696-5a59-89b3-efcd248b7a09" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z &=-2 \\\\ x+2y+2z &=1 \\\\ y+z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form. Select the resulting augmented matrix." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757044 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "089ad372-a6b6-5012-bd8e-5c495f4c959e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-4,-3,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757035} {:answer/id #uuid "249a25e5-ceda-5203-864b-6eaa4d067123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4,1,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757041} {:answer/id #uuid "48968c25-d43d-5f47-91b8-9267e029e085" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-6,-5,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757045} {:answer/id #uuid "93a9d4e5-b102-5a05-a5cc-47bb0c3166b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(2,-1,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757054} {:answer/id #uuid "acec38ec-694b-519c-b34a-94534ef14fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4,0,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93a9d4e5-b102-5a05-a5cc-47bb0c3166b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(2,-1,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757054} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce713a4-3738-58c2-a5eb-e1cb65fe41b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757048}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43d434df-4fe0-572f-8092-df01f458b6f0" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-z &=2 \\\\ -x+2y+2z &=0 \\\\ -x+3y+2z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=2 \\\\ y &=1-(1)(2) \\\\ &=-1 \\\\ x &=2-(-2)(-1) \\\\ &\\quad -(-1)(2) \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(2,-1,2\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "035ff279-287b-5828-b15c-1d53b40ed674" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(3,1,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757034} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba9a4f4-3c9d-5b75-8192-c332c987359f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(5,2,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757050} {:answer/id #uuid "702898dc-5152-5d90-94f5-60a19634fe7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1,0,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757051} {:answer/id #uuid "8137113d-8174-59e4-93da-b3c06683c8af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-4,-5,3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757053} {:answer/id #uuid "d21007a3-ac69-5467-b531-244c4d19d5cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,-3,3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "702898dc-5152-5d90-94f5-60a19634fe7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1,0,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757051} :answer-field/id #uuid "097cf6cf-7ab0-500b-8e9c-53820a0e7fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757036}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6575f85d-7aac-53f1-b121-353f331e6bc9" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-z &=3 \\\\ x-2y &=1 \\\\ x-y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=-2 \\\\ y &=-2-(1)(-2) \\\\ &=0 \\\\ x &=3-(-2)(0) \\\\ &\\quad -(-1)(-2) \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(1,0,-2\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10250073-5db8-5db8-9c61-1b21f1c54a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1,-1,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757038} {:answer/id #uuid "1538c7c1-bb2e-58b1-a917-9abe40e0d6c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1,-1,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757039} {:answer/id #uuid "3d2fcba7-0ed6-573b-a7b8-e9b4e94f3d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(2,0,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757043} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4c2928-d48d-5b6d-a5e9-9d887d060158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-2,-4,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757057} {:answer/id #uuid "f95152d0-f704-551b-aa50-33665d332b7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-1,-3,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10250073-5db8-5db8-9c61-1b21f1c54a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1,-1,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757038} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce659242-8034-5ea4-8706-058cb83ef478" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757061}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5bdf71e-ebab-5543-be28-3273bcd44d39" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ for the variables $x,y,z$ in that order.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=-3 \\\\ y &=-1-(0)(-3) \\\\ &=-1 \\\\ x &=2-(-1)(-1) \\\\ &\\quad -(0)(-3) \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(1,-1,-3\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "161cd6fb-ac5e-5a01-91a0-06b484f89777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-1,1,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757040} {:answer/id #uuid "26a90c42-55a7-59bb-ad2a-afe53c2bd562" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-1,2,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757042} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd69249-d4e3-5078-bbb4-c73f3bd521f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-5,5,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757052} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fae520-1c87-594a-b53b-202e6d359909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4,-3,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757059} {:answer/id #uuid "db7ee354-f98e-54ae-b1be-4b825ca4b056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-3,3,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8fae520-1c87-594a-b53b-202e6d359909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4,-3,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757059} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd7e3223-cf2d-57a0-81c7-2a28c58e1717" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757060}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec343d89-4a32-5dd8-9fa7-33e20598d3b0" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-z &=3 \\\\ -x-y+2z &=-5 \\\\ y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=-2 \\\\ y &=-3-(0)(-2) \\\\ &=-3 \\\\ x &=3-(1)(-3) \\\\ &\\quad -(-1)(-2) \\\\ &=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(4,-3,-2\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757070 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59a0edf1-af6b-5428-aec1-b7b5ed58ef26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757081} {:answer/id #uuid "6a00caa2-399c-52a8-b0fd-a0f6bcad7566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757084} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4e0828-da20-58d4-be26-e8f7c5ee3b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757086} {:answer/id #uuid "c74a2354-e3ba-57cb-b308-2f259c1b74c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757094} {:answer/id #uuid "e8a994ee-f7b5-5b9f-bad7-38c21826bffd" :answer/typ