erset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{c}=\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda \\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{b},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\lambda =2\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30a0045e-f1f3-57fa-89c6-bd1617062077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30a0045e-f1f3-57fa-89c6-bd1617062077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300196} :answer-field/id #uuid "a550aade-6952-55e1-9a53-4cfddf1f7e28" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301759}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d63f1783-5306-55e3-b17e-74d8a2e39050" :question/math-academy-id "q-327049" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a43139fc26d5778c40db020a7ebc9122c2fd54c0dcd4eb44cfd1671936a4055a.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b},$ then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $2\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we first draw the vector $2\\mathbf{b}$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/1d/1d266a8324d18191f5bc8560be6539d54d1a11916f33ead7432d9f528769fc22.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $2\\mathbf{b}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=\\frac{1}{2}|\\mathbf{a}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $\\mathbf{a}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}.$\