1c2fa850924f446c6f086dcacd170f1ca6d24.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-\\mathbf{b}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=2.5|\\mathbf{a}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-2.5\\mathbf{a}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{c} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{b}-2.5\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}=-2.5\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{a},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2.5\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235582 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab5b44a-6f14-5d8c-b994-0ff723092bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234586} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5b4c72-e340-52b5-be53-6903f63361a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234611} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe36434-9519-583f-9b69-c587e4937715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234866} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1ea7c1-61ca-56ba-a7d9-91573e3d6a5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234869} {:answer/id #uuid "f46ca5b6-1fd3-597e-9657-e4197a5f9d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ab5b44a-6f14-5d8c-b994-0ff723092bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234586} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aa48e98-a238-5102-8717-85e261cb4e21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234997}] :question/difficulty {:db/ide